{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help","id":1095319,"title":"Chronicle Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-21T18:43:41-07:00","id":1095319,"title":"Chronicle Help","content":"I thought I'd create a thread similar to the ask a simple question thread, but more focused on setting and chronicle help, so please feel free to ask your own questions regarding getting help for your chronicles.<br /> <br /> I started my 2nd 2e Chronicle today, also based in Boston (because I know it, having run 60 sessions in Boston over the years).<br /> <br /> I have two players that have chosen workable concepts: Obrimos Perfected Adept &amp; Moros Necromancer Investigator.<br /> <br /> My third player has a really strange character concept: Acanthus junk-art scrapper with Matter as his 3rd Arcana and a rank 2 Raven familiar that is a Spirit of Greed. He's in the Adamantine Arrow and wanted his own Sanctum &amp; Hallow (2 dots) which is a Sacred Tree in the secluded area of a city park.<br /> <br /> I know it's off the wall, but this player really wants all this eclectic stuff and I really believe in letting people play the characters they want to play.<br /> <br /> He's never played a WoD game before and I'd really like to figure out how to make this character work. Here are my questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Can a Raven Greed spirit make any sense?<br /> <br /> 2. Can a Sanctum based around a Sacred Tree in the middle of Boston Commons park make any sense? How can this be a Safe Place, for instance?<br /> <br /> 3. Is there an Acanthus Legacy with Matter as a 3rd Arcana make any sense?<br /> <br /> I'd really appreciate assistance making this jumble of stuff all fit together somehow, because let's face it: The idea of an Acanthus Arrow Junk-artist Matter mage tasked with protecting a Sacred Tree with his Raven Spirit could be very cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 05-21-2017, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T20:23:49-07:00","id":1095340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help#post1095319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Can a Raven Greed spirit make any sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>A spirit like that makes perfect sense. I wouldn't consider it <i>magath</i> since greed is associated with ravens naturally. Then again, the Awakened are much more forgiving of <i>magath</i> than, say, the Forsaken are.<br /> <br /> As a Familiar you have three options - a Rank 1 greed spirit that looks like a raven (one dot of Influence: Greed), a Rank 1 raven spirit that behaves greedily (one dot of Influence: Ravens), and a Rank 2 raven-greed spirit that probably used to be one of the former two (one dot each of Influence: Greed and Influence: Ravens)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Can a Sanctum based around a Sacred Tree in the middle of Boston Commons park make any sense? How can this be a Safe Place, for instance? </div> </div> </div>Well... can the character somehow prevent people from coming to the tree? I'd say no. I'd just say there's a secret underground bunker or something under the tree, and have that be the Safe Place and Sanctum. The tree itself can be the focal point of a Hallow.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And about the sacred tree Sanctum, it just occurred to me that the Acanthus are associated with fairies, and fairies are associated with mounds and underground kingdoms beneath such mounds. And hey, there are plenty of hilltops where they have trees growing on them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Is there an Acanthus Legacy with Matter as a 3rd Arcana make any sense? </div> </div> </div>There isn't any Path - 3rd Ruling Arcana combination that shouldn't be able to make sense. A junk scrapper may be initiated into or develop a Legacy that enchants seemingly worthless junk into mundanely useful items and supernaturally lucky charms.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Or a Legacy that magically enhances the durability of objects so that they can bear the weight of time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 05-21-2017, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T20:57:32-07:00","id":1095345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1095340#post1095340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Familiar you have three options - a Rank 1 greed spirit that looks like a raven (one dot of Influence: Greed), a Rank 1 raven spirit that behaves greedily (one dot of Influence: Ravens), and a Rank 2 raven-greed spirit that probably used to be one of the former two (one dot each of Influence: Greed and Influence: Ravens)</div> </div> </div> </div>You've also got Option Four: Any of the above Fettered to a raven.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well... can the character somehow prevent people from coming to the tree? I'd say no. I'd just say there's a secret underground bunker or something under the tree, and have that be the Safe Place and Sanctum. </div> </div> </div>This seems an excellent place to point out that Spirit Manses count as Safe Places and the possession of a Familiar without dots in Spirit most readily suggests a Mentor with the Arcanum. (It could also suggest run-of-the-mill Status requisitions, but concrete characters are a little easier to keep track of.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T21:09:07-07:00","id":1095349,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the help. How do Spirit Manses work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T21:14:15-07:00","id":1095351,"title":"","content":"Oh, I completely forgot about Fettering and Spirit Manses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks for the help. How do Spirit Manses work? </div> </div> </div>For its Duration, the Spirit Manse spell creates a Place-That-Is-Not (a location in the Shadow that does not correspond a location in the physical world). It acts as a Safe Place with dots equal to the spell's Potency. The mage decides the Manse's form, but it is colored by the symbolism of her Path and Nimbus.<br /> <br /> For a Reach, the caster adds an Iris that connects the Manse to the physical world. This makes the spell Withstood by Gauntlet Strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T22:30:34-07:00","id":1095366,"title":"","content":"It sounds awesome, but why would a Master of Spirit go to the trouble of creating a Spirit Manse near this Sacred Tree so that a starting Acanthus could guard it and use it as a Hallow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T22:36:57-07:00","id":1095368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1095351#post1095351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a Reach, the caster adds an Iris that connects the Manse to the physical world. This makes the spell Withstood by Gauntlet Strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, this latter fact combined with the specification of the tree being in &quot;the secluded area&quot; of the park might be decent grounds to have the place be built into a minor locus \u2014 perhaps the Manse is a hollow space for storage; depending on how much you feel like tying the familiar and the Sanctum together, perhaps the locus is conceptually resonant with the spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T00:23:20-07:00","id":1095395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1095366#post1095366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds awesome, but why would a Master of Spirit go to the trouble of creating a Spirit Manse near this Sacred Tree so that a starting Acanthus could guard it and use it as a Hallow?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps he's your hands off mentor who's letting you use his resources, in exchange for protecting it.<br /> Perhaps it was some other Mage's, but he moved on from the city and you claimed it.<br /> Perhaps it's always been like that, and you claimed it when you found it.<br /> Perhaps you did him a favour, and he spend the Willpower dot to safely relinquish such a spell in payment.<br /> <br /> Mages have an economy of favours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":".  Other ideas 05-22-2017, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T04:58:35-07:00","id":1095444,"title":"","content":"No need for a mentor character to build it for you. It's entirely possible that the sacred tree in question is at the heart of a naturally occurring verge.<br /> <br /> Better yet - make it into a Mystery. Turn this unusual sanctum into a plot hook. There's an Iris in the tree leading to Another Place, somewhere the character can retreat when they need somewhere safe but that they're still exploring and don't entirely understand (my vote would be the Road of a dead archmaster).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5958-logocentric","name":"Logocentric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T13:01:57-07:00","id":1097599,"title":"","content":"If we are gonna have this be open to lots of new questions.<br /> <br /> Q4: My new games first story covers digging through a creepy old house, which will go on to become the groups Sanctum. What can I fill it with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T13:57:48-07:00","id":1097619,"title":"","content":"Creepy house covers a lot of territory. Ghosts or spirits are appropriate naturally, it could be an old sanctum covered in warped spells left behind by the Mage who lived there previously and died suddenly, or there could be an Abyssal taint on the place. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T14:37:17-07:00","id":1097622,"title":"","content":"What reason does the players have to choose that particular location for their Sanctum? If it's that one of them inherited the place and neither wants the Sanctum to be at their personal home then anything could go on in that old house, but otherwise you'd have to give them a reason to want to put up their Sanctum there. Once you have that reason you can put complications in place based on that reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T19:56:41-07:00","id":1099726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logocentric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1095444#post1095444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No need for a mentor character to build it for you. It's entirely possible that the sacred tree in question is at the heart of a naturally occurring verge.<br /> <br /> Better yet - make it into a Mystery. Turn this unusual sanctum into a plot hook. There's an Iris in the tree leading to Another Place, somewhere the character can retreat when they need somewhere safe but that they're still exploring and don't entirely understand (my vote would be the Road of a dead archmaster).</div> </div> </div> </div>Any chance this might work as a safe place in The Hedge or an Arcadian Verge instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T22:24:09-07:00","id":1099758,"title":"","content":"Yeah, anArcadian Verge would be fine. I wouldn't make it connected to the Hedge though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T08:14:13-07:00","id":1099827,"title":"","content":"Ok. What would be a nice way to tie in the Raven/Greed Spirit if I go with the Arcadian Verge idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T13:23:12-07:00","id":1099900,"title":"","content":"Would it be too much to have an Acanthus Mentor that's never around,<br /> but actually leaves an array of passive-aggressive sticky-notes to guide their pupil?<br /> Likely due to them abusing Prophecy to read their pupil's moves and leaving notes in the right spots.<br /> Twist being they've actually been dead for months and have laid out a lot of sticky-notes before death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T15:34:34-07:00","id":1099933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1099900#post1099900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be too much to have an Acanthus Mentor that's never around,<br /> but actually leaves an array of passive-aggressive sticky-notes to guide their pupil?<br /> Likely due to them abusing Prophecy to read their pupil's moves and leaving notes in the right spots.<br /> Twist being they've actually been dead for months and have laid out a lot of sticky-notes before death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, seems very Acanthus. Mind you the mentor's ultimate plan might be to have his student go back in time and prevent his death. Acanthus, they plan for everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T04:21:48-07:00","id":1100068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1099900#post1099900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be too much to have an Acanthus Mentor that's never around,<br /> but actually leaves an array of passive-aggressive sticky-notes to guide their pupil?<br /> Likely due to them abusing Prophecy to read their pupil's moves and leaving notes in the right spots.<br /> Twist being they've actually been dead for months and have laid out a lot of sticky-notes before death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like what an elderly Acanthus Sphinx member would do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T06:45:57-07:00","id":1100427,"title":"","content":"I appreciate all the help guys. The challenge for me with this player is that unlike most players in my games he really knows what he wants, which is good, but he doesn't know the setting as it's his first CoD game. So giving him what he wants in a setting compatible way is the tough part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T05:10:33-07:00","id":1102237,"title":"","content":"I have an idea for a story that requires a constant air of tension between the pentacle and the seers.<br /> What's shiny enough to make every mage in a city tiptoe like ballerinas in an infinite expanse of egg shells?<br /> <br /> I've been thinking maybe a relic that has immense potency,<br /> or a sarira left by an exarch/oracle,<br /> perhaps even an ochemata that forgot its purpose and became a normal mortal.<br /> <br /> Toying with those concepts. Which one has the most potential though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T11:22:52-07:00","id":1102310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1102237#post1102237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an idea for a story that requires a constant air of tension between the pentacle and the seers.<br /> What's shiny enough to make every mage in a city tiptoe like ballerinas in an infinite expanse of egg shells?<br /> <br /> I've been thinking maybe a relic that has immense potency,<br /> or a sarira left by an exarch/oracle,<br /> perhaps even an ochemata that forgot its purpose and became a normal mortal.<br /> <br /> Toying with those concepts. Which one has the most potential though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like the Shadow Concord. Likely Fate enforced. Break the rules and get cursed to oblivion. Rules regulating outright engagements, with little actual knowledge of the whole deal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T13:56:13-07:00","id":1102603,"title":"","content":"So I thought I'd share how the Acanthus in my game turned out:<br /> <br /> He ended up trading in Sanctum and Hallow for Mentor 2.<br /> <br /> He's still guarding a sacred tree in Malcolm X park in Boston, with his Grandfather (also Acanthus) Mentor. They live in a nearby apartment together.<br /> <br /> For his familiar he decided on a Rank 2 Spirit of Greed. It possessed a Raven junk-art sculpture and we gave it a form of Possess called Inanimate Possession. Seem ok?<br /> <br /> Lastly, he really wanted a Hearthstone that could transport him back to the Sacred Tree, but he only had 2 merit dots left. I allowed him a limited Co-Location (Space 3), keyed to his bloodline, only for travelling back to the Sacred Tree. I thought that 2 dots was reasonable for this. What does everyone think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 06-11-2017, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T14:52:58-07:00","id":1102617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1102603#post1102603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For his familiar he decided on a Rank 2 Spirit of Greed. It possessed a Raven junk-art sculpture and we gave it a form of Possess called Inanimate Possession. Seem ok?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possess already works on objects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T10:28:33-07:00","id":1104354,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> <br /> One of my players is a Moros (Death 3, Matter 1, Mind 2) private investigator. He's in the Free Council, which Dave likes to call the Order of &quot;human culture&quot;. This player isn't really interested in cultural trappings in his magic, but likes the private investigator angle. Is this sufficiently of &quot;human culture&quot; to quality as a good FC character concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T11:00:20-07:00","id":1104373,"title":"","content":"Give him a fedora and a Ferrari or an inverness cape.<br /> \u200bPlay up a cultural stereotype of the P.I. and it should fit. It should even have obvious Yantra ideas.<br /> He shouldn't have to totally recreate the stereotype, just incorporate elements that society commonly associates with the idea of a P.I..<br /> \u200bEven something as small as carrying a steno note pad can play into it, just as long as the average joe recognizes what he is without deep investigation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 06-16-2017, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T11:11:03-07:00","id":1104377,"title":"","content":"It's a perfectly fine Free Council character. Generally if a player wants to be in an Order, they've got all the justification they need already. If he wanted, he could take Techne to draw on the art and science of criminal investigation itself as a magical tool, but even that's not necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T17:08:38-07:00","id":1104541,"title":"","content":"I imagine that private investigators are at least a sub-culture unto themselves, and then there's definitely fandom of the noir style that romanticized them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T15:41:01-07:00","id":1104885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1104541#post1104541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that private investigators are at least a sub-culture unto themselves, and then there's definitely fandom of the noir style that romanticized them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mage: Noir book might be a useful read even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T11:26:45-07:00","id":1106661,"title":"","content":"Thanks again for the responses.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think ahead and anticipate potential issues for me as a Storyteller, since my main weakness is coming up with stuff on the fly.<br /> <br /> To that end, my Acanthus has chosen Gateway as one of the Numina for his Greed Spirit Familiar. At some point the group is going to get into a situation where they want to flee into The Shadow. I'd like to make this doable, but dangerous. Do you guys have any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T11:42:54-07:00","id":1106665,"title":"","content":"Gateway is a Manifestation Condition, not a Numena, as such the only areas the Familiar can open a Gateway in are areas that are Resonant and Open for a greed spirit. So it's pretty likely their will be dangerous greedy entities on -either- side of the gate. From low level drug dealers looking for a big score to a dragon nesting on its hoard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T18:26:48-07:00","id":1106818,"title":"","content":"I take it a Spirit mage could get around this by making anywhere Open essentially?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T01:57:50-07:00","id":1106920,"title":"","content":"A Spirit Mage can cause a Resonant area to be Open at two dots, so it would still have to be a place that's Resonance matched with the greed familiar. At three dots of Spirit a Mage can essentially create a Gateway themselves.<br /> <br /> By the way, the Essence cost for Gateway is pretty steep, it would be perfectly in character for a greed spirit to be unwilling to spend it because after all, its greedy.<br /> <br /> Also, the Gateway condition remains for an entire scene and anyone or anything can go wandering through that thing which should provide ample opportunity for complications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T06:25:21-07:00","id":1108367,"title":"","content":"Ok. Can't the Spirit just shut it down when it wants though?<br /> <br /> Also, the situation came up where my players were fighting The Shinje and the Moros in my group decided to send him into Twilight with Ghost Gate. Is there really no Withstand for this? I mean, it didn't matter because The Shinje had Death 5 from claiming Khatvanga anyway, so it just came back on the following turn. This seems a little broken to me. I'm probably going to rule that it uses Withstand when targeting someone. What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> Withstand isn't necessarily going to make all the difference, but right now at Death 3 all it takes is Reach for Sensory, Instant and Advanced Duration and you can send a powerful antagonist into Twilight for a week. Your tool will take the Paradox to a chance die.<br /> <br /> Adding the Withstand necessitates changing the Primary factor to Potency and taking a -2 or -4 dice penalty (to overcome a 3 or 4 resistance trait), which in turn pretty much requires the PC spend WP to make it happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 06-27-2017, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T06:41:21-07:00","id":1108378,"title":"","content":"The rules don't say if the spirit that creates the Gateway can shut it when they wish, they say that it stays open for a scene. You could allow it to shut it down though. The main point was to address the fact that you wanted the spirit to be able to use Gateway, but wanted options for making it doable, but dangerous.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why you'd think Ghost Gate is broken. If you use the basic version of the spell you still have to force the potential subject through the gate and though that's a permanent transformation you now have a pissed off enemy who can wander around interacting with ghosts gaining allies or minions and one of them can probably help him get back out of Twilight. If you're using the Reach clause to automatically transfer a subject to Twilight, that will only last as long as the spell and it's unlikely that in combat you could push the spell's Duration far enough to be more than an inconvenience for the subject, they will be back. <br /> <br /> That said it makes sense that a spell like that used as an offensive option would be subject to Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T06:46:55-07:00","id":1108381,"title":"","content":"It's easy to make it last a week. See my edits above. But I think I'm going to rule that Withstand is necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T21:44:32-08:00","id":1162901,"title":"","content":"I have a new dilemma in my main game.<br /> <br /> The Thyrsus Silver Ladder in my group really doesn't like spending the Mana for his Matter spells so is interested in joining a Matter Primary Legacy to get around these costs.<br /> <br /> The character was a Zoo-to-you guy before he Awakened. His familiar is a Spirit Bear and the cabal's sanctum is a underneath an old bear den that is no longer in use. He has a lot of social skills and high survival.<br /> <br /> His play style tends to favor Life spells though - Web of Life is a Praxis, Honing the Form, and Transform Life are big favorites. He's mainly used Matter for Remote Control.<br /> <br /> Do you have any suggestions of what might fit and make sense?<br /> <br /> He's not a power gamer. He's a 12 year old boy that just wants to grow tentacles, give himself +3 strength and occasional unlock doors with Remote Control. LOL.<br /> <br /> But it would be nice if we could come up with some way of getting what he wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T22:52:55-08:00","id":1162911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1162901#post1162901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Thyrsus Silver Ladder in my group really doesn't like spending the Mana for his Matter spells so is interested in joining a Matter Primary Legacy to get around these costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, considering the narrative legwork that Legacies entail, it feels like the better investment in the immediate term is just picking up Matter spells as new or extra Praxes or pursue them as rotes \u2014 a Legacy is something you'd ideally want to seed the core framework of as befits the source of a major decision about what the character is going to be, and that's going to call for a bit more of a concentrated focus than &quot;having to spend Mana on Matter spells is inconvenient.&quot;<br /> <br /> Outside the context of unlocking doors, does he have any preferred aesthetics for his Matter spells in the same way that you've alluded to his applications of Life?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T23:55:12-08:00","id":1162919,"title":"","content":"A quick search brings up Lords of the Inanimate, a Thyrsus Legacy with Matter who awaken the spirits of objects and devices over them. It's a Silver Ladder Legacy as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T07:00:04-08:00","id":1162990,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I've decided that I'm going to talk with him about the direction of his character and convince him that if he's not going to go heavy into Matter that it doesn't make sense to get a Matter based Legacy.<br /> <br /> I actually think Orphans of Proteus probably makes the most sense for him. He's just tired of being Mana starved.<br /> <br /> The only other idea I had was something centered around Blood, as it's a liquid and can be manipulated with Matter, but still has Life symbolism as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T20:18:52-08:00","id":1168466,"title":"","content":"So in my Boston 3.0 chronicle I have a character who is searching for his brother who has joined the Cult of the Red Word. He is also searching for a Jade pendant that last was last in the possession of the brother. They managed to find out that the pendant was recently bought at a pawn shop by a French professional woman.<br /> <br /> I need help figuring out what the pendant is, why the brother sold it to the pawn shop, and why the French woman wanted it (less critical since she just might have liked how it looked even).<br /> <br /> It would be cool if it were related to the Prince of 100,000 Leaves.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T21:13:53-08:00","id":1168473,"title":"","content":"Long, long ago the first group of European Mages to settle in the Boston area were in danger of being wiped out by native Mages and allied hunger spirits. Fortunately for the Europeans one of their number knew of a ritual that could save them but she refused to share, preferring to be killed by the natives. Her fellows held different priorities and forced her to tell, then sacrificed her in casting the ritual which somehow rewrote their reality causing the defeat of the natives.<br /> Those Mages still died of causes other than old age, the last one being eaten by the first members of the Cult of the Red Word and he was a willing meal and possibly the cult's founder.<br /> \u200bHave it turn out the pendant belonged to that poor Mage sacrificed by her fellows, perhaps even be part of the ritual that took her life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T09:16:20-08:00","id":1168541,"title":"","content":"It's good, but I forgot to tell you that these characters are from Korea. Also, why would the Cult want to sell the pendant to the pawn shop?<br /> <br /> I appreciate the help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T15:00:08-08:00","id":1168647,"title":"","content":"1. The shop is used by the Red Word Cult to collect errant Leaves - like the Jade Pendant. After all, when people find antiques they might just decide to sell them. However, information on the sale and the involvement of the Frenchwoman weren't supposed to get out. This suggests someone infiltrated them and helped the information along. The other possibility is that the Cult accidentally let their holy relic be sold to a random person, which means an innocent woman is now in danger.<br /> <br /> 2. The Cult believed the Pendant to be one of the Leaves, but upon inspection they realized it wasn't the case, so they sold it. This was a mistake on their part. The Jade Pendant is the last remaining link to its original owner - a woman who knew how the Abyssal Intrusion worked and how it could have been handled. It might be due to Sympathetic links, it might be her Ghostly Anchor, or it might even be her Soulstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T06:31:05-08:00","id":1168787,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that the Jade Pendant is a Soul Stone.<br /> <br /> I'm just trying to piece it all together:<br /> <br /> - PC's brother was somehow drawn to Boston from Korea with the Pendant, joined the Red Word and was told to sell it to the pawn shop for &quot;distribution&quot;<br /> - French woman (also a cultist) bought the Pendant with the intention of bringing it to Montreal to a Scelesti in the Cult.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking the Soul Stone contains a Legacy used by Scelesti that worship the Prince and the Scelesti in Montreal wishes to learn this Legacy from the Stone, which has been passed around the globe by the Red Word for centuries for said purpose.<br /> <br /> Questions:<br /> <br /> What do you think this Legacy should be? Why would Scelesti in the Cult of the Red Word want to learn it? How did the Pendant end up in the PC's family? Why did his brother join the Red Word (he may have joined before coming to Boston, actually)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 12-19-2017, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T14:50:52-08:00","id":1168929,"title":"","content":"You can draw upon preexisting Scelesti Legacies or modify legitimate ones to fit within the Prince's imagery. It's possible that someone on the forum already updated some of these to 2nd Edition, but you would have to check:<br /> <br /> 1st Edition Corebook Scelesti<br /> They can essentially be left &quot;as is&quot;. Their Attainments already corrupt Spirits into Abyssal forms. You would only need to acknowledge that their gradual warping leads to the 100.000 Leaves ideal. Time being their Optional Arcanum fits with the Prince being a Time Anomaly and lends itself well to dread Prophecies.<br /> <br /> Anti-Choir of Hashmallim<br /> Instead of summoning an Angel of the Aether each Legate can call upon a Gulmoth or Acamoth of the Prince to act as both teacher and servant. You could repurpose the Sanctifier from your other campaign or make a few Intruders of your own.<br /> <br /> The Hunter's Flesh<br /> Because of the Prince's symbolism the Red Word version of the Legacy would likely resonate with Obrimos instead of Thyrsus - regal instead of primal. They could also have a connection to Hunger sufferers, as shepherds of abominations.<br /> <br /> Anti-Unforgotten Scions<br /> Essentially as written but propagating Abyssal knowledge as far and wide as they can get away with. Not only do they have good synergy with Leaves, they would also enable unAwakened cultists to use supernatural powers, which puts the players against more perilous odds.<br /> <br /> Anti-Secret Order of the Gate<br /> Instead of entering the Place Between, they can temporarily enter their patron Annunaku. It's a clear gamechanger, since this allows for direct cooperation between the timelines.<br /> <br /> You could also approach it from an opposite angle:<br /> <br /> 11th Question<br /> A legitimate Legacy of investigators, subverted to search for pieces of the Prince. Basically, you could use any Right-Handed Legacy and set up conflict between it's respectable and Abyssal branches.<br /> <br /> Logophages<br /> The original owner of the Pendant actively worked against the Prince. The cultists hope to interrogate the Mage's Ghost or utilize the Legacy's penchant for investigation, but are toying with something that could undo them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 12-19-2017, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T11:15:05-08:00","id":1169148,"title":"","content":"These are all really good idea and I think I'll go with Scelesti as it's probably the simplest way to go. I'll call the Prince version The Rightful Kings or something like that.<br /> <br /> If you have a second to help still, I'm still trying to figure out the following: How did the Pendant end up in the PC's family? Why did his brother join the Red Word (he may have joined before coming to Boston, actually)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T15:05:04-08:00","id":1169205,"title":"","content":"These questions concern the family of one of the PC's, so the answers should heavily depend on that player's preferences. In a way, these NPCs are an extension of his character, so earning his approval is especially important.<br /> <br /> How did the family get the Pendant:<br /> 1. Korea is the site of a minor Prince of 100.000 Leaves intrusion and the family has had history with local Scelesti. Either as allies or enemies.<br /> 2. Sheer happenstance. Maybe they bought it on an auction. Maybe they found it while digging a ditch. These things happen.<br /> <br /> His brother might have joined the red Word due to:<br /> 1. Dissatisfaction with his life leading to being ensnared by the cult. You can introduce family drama this way.<br /> 2. Being influenced by the Soulstone - Horcrux style. You can borrow from Harry Potter and see if your players spot it.<br /> 3. Having been coerced by the Cult, once they've found about the Pendant. The question is, is the brother willing to defect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T21:26:33-08:00","id":1169269,"title":"","content":"This player is super easy going and will be happy with whatever I decide.<br /> <br /> I think the fact that he knew his brother was going to Boston and then lost contact with him after the fact suggests that he joined the Red Word after coming to Boston, otherwise he would have covered his tracks better.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that the pendant attracted the attention of the cult somehow. Maybe Zechariah Crowther noticed it at some function as something he had read about in one of the Leaves he was collecting and informed Wendigo in Waltman's Neck who then learned the Legacy from the pendant and passed it along to the Mage in Montreal via the French Canadian woman.<br /> <br /> I could just have the brother be dead and killed for the pendant by Z's sister Annie, but if I want the PC's brother in the cult what do you think a logical recruitment might be like and why would they undertake that recruitment instead of just murdering him for the pendant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T05:50:37-08:00","id":1169322,"title":"","content":"Let me think...<br /> <br /> 1. Their family actually has some connection to Scelesti. If they're allies, the Cult feels obliged to bring him in as a new member. If they're enemies, they want to keep him close as leverage.<br /> 2. The Soulstone has somehow rubbed off on the brother (Horcrux!), or at least the Cult think it did. They also feel that even though he can't keep the Pendant, they don't want to kill off someone so blessed.<br /> 3. The brother makes an ordinary emotional connection with someone from the Cult, not knowing who he's dealing with. That person decides to &quot;save&quot; him bring him to the &quot;right&quot; side.<br /> <br /> The actual recruitment could rely on classic cult tactics, from love-bombing to gradual desensitization. It could also be misguided and rely on direct coercion and threats, making the brother eager to defect. People more knowledgeable than me wrote mountains of papers on the subject.<br /> <br /> As an extra observation: If the Pendant originates from the Prince, this means someone took a chunk of the Abyss and made a Soulstone out of it. This sounds like an edge case that begs for unexpected consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T08:54:50-08:00","id":1169369,"title":"","content":"Ok. I think that will work really well. I have enough to go on now. I'll probably leave the decision about whether or not the brother is in the cult to the last minute depending on what I think will be best for the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T18:01:54-08:00","id":1171382,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">So here's where I'm at with it. I'm interested in critiques or improvements or more ideas.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Jade Pendant: Eye of Ammut the Devourer</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- Soul Stone of Ihy, an Egyptian Scelesti worshiper of the Prince of 100,000 Leaves that crafted the stone directly from Abyssal matter found in the alternate history </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- The Rightful Kings Legacy can be learned from the Jade Pendant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- The Eye \u201cencourages\u201d the owner to \u201cgift\u201d it to a loved one. That loved one then becomes the target of the owner\u2019s hunger and over years the compulsion grows until that lover is killed and consumed in a cannibalistic ritual</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Path of the Pendant</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- Originated in Egypt. Soul Stone of Ihy, Vizier to Pharaoh Unas, last of the 5th Dynasty</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- Upon his death it was stolen by tomb robbers and sold to an Indian merchant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- It slowly made its way over the intervening centuries to South Korea</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- Eventually it was purchased as an anniversary present in an antiquities auction by Balam\u2019s great grandfather in 1934</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- It was passed down to the eldest son to be given to his wife and upon her death her first son etc\u2026</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- Balam (PC) was the next in line to receive it, but his younger brother secretly took it as it resonated particularly strongly with the Abyssal Shard in his soul and he coveted its mysteries</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- When it was discovered missing, Balam was charged by his father with retrieving it and bringing his younger sibling home</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- Zechariah Crowther noticed the Eye of Ammut at a social function worn by the brother\u2019s girlfriend. It matched a description in one of the Leaves he had collected and read</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- He immediately informed Wendigo in Waltman\u2019s Neck who requested that Zee and Annie bring the couple in with the pendant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- Zee and Annie went to retrieve the pendant and discovered the brother in the act of killing his girlfriend (accelerated time frame due to stronger resonance) in a manner befitting the Eye and used it as an opportunity to recruit him into the Red Word</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- Wendigo took the Eye and learned Ihy\u2019s Legacy from it and then instructed Zee to sell it to Suffolk Jewellers &amp; Pawnbrokers</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- He then informed Roi du Sang in Montreal about his good fortune and where he could send his Sleepwalker Red Word assistant Genevieve Tremblay to acquire the Stone</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- She purchased the Pendant from Suffolk\u2019s, brought it to her master where it was scrubbed for Sympathetic connections and is now being used to spread Ihy\u2019s Legacy to Scelesti there.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T18:45:34-08:00","id":1171399,"title":"","content":"So the question remains why it was sold to the pawn shop. Maybe Wendigo had it sent there as the pawn shop had no direct connection to him and he worried about the pendant's influence? Or maybe he needed it in an innocuous hiding spot when the heat was suddenly turned up on him? If the latter you could have some fun with a Boston cabal that's currently going through the plot of Gloria Mundi (I think I got the name right) and he had the pendant sent off when they came looking for Sloth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T12:04:46-08:00","id":1171583,"title":"","content":"Good ideas. I think I'm going to have the pawnshop just be a convenient place for the exchange to happen without Zee having to give the item to Genevieve directly.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, no one in the cabal has Time so I don't have to worry about Postcog like you usually do in Mage. Three of my four players have Mind 2+ though and using Perfect Recall for accurate witness testimony is fairly popular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 12-29-2017, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T13:51:23-08:00","id":1186062,"title":"","content":"So I have a new player Aspiration that I'm trying to get prepared for.<br /> <br /> Baron Draugr, the Moros of my group (Gnosis 2, Death 3, Mind 2, Matter 1) is very interested in Ghosts and Souls.<br /> <br /> He moved to Boston with his sister and opened a private detective agency. His sister was killed, which resulted in his Awakening when he saw her ghost briefly before it sank into the Underworld.<br /> <br /> He's left it open ended as to why she was killed, but he suspects it was an enemy that he made as a detective. His Aspiration is to find out why she was murdered and by whom?<br /> <br /> I've made her a historical tour guide at the closed Danvers Asylum, which is former Tremere territory.<br /> <br /> I've decided to make her someone that ran afoul of Mama Desta and or Ahriman (of the Ebon Noose, which I've made a Tremere wannabe) and that is why she was killed.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for advice on what precipitated her murder.<br /> <br /> Just so you know, I've created Danvers from scratch in a previous Chronicle and thought it useful to re-use the material I had made. You can read the first 3 sessions here: <a href=\"https://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log/session-thirty-eight\" target=\"_blank\">https://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal...n-thirty-eight</a><br /> <br /> It's populated by fleshed out Ghosts that have ways of resolving their anchors, but Mama Desta has left Judge Hawthorne's Ghost (of Salem Witch Trial fame) possessed by an Inferno Demon in charge of the place with his Ghost lieutenants. They mostly operate out of the abandoned wing where the Tremere vault is located. Inside the vault is N'thraka the 9th Calamity from Intruders, surrounded by radioactive soul stones to keep him bound. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Why might his sister have been murdered?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 02-14-2018, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T14:40:24-08:00","id":1186076,"title":"","content":"1. One of the Ghosts, perhaps even Judge Hawthorne, tried to use the sister in their plans. It could have been malignant, or maybe just to escape slavery. Either way the Tremere found out about the plan and killed her to make a point. Perhaps they even said to the Ghosts - &quot;Look what you made us do&quot;.<br /> <br /> 2. Ahriman impulsively stole the sister's Soul. Her sudden deterioration could have attracted attention towards the asylum, so the Tremere did damage control by killing her. This wasn't a well thought-out plan and the problem could have been better solved by returning the Soul, but who cares about some Sleeper anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T10:24:53-08:00","id":1186348,"title":"","content":"I like both of these ideas. I'm trying to decide between them.<br /> <br /> I think I'll go with the first one, as it leads more directly to Danvers for which I have a wealth of material prepared.<br /> <br /> A ghost from Danvers possessed her in order to escape servitude. After going home one night it killed her in the hopes that it would not travel back with her to work (Danvers). What do you think might happen to the ghost afterwards? Would it snap back to its anchor at Danvers anyway? What other possibilities could there be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T13:42:10-08:00","id":1186396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1186348#post1186348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like both of these ideas. I'm trying to decide between them.<br /> <br /> I think I'll go with the first one, as it leads more directly to Danvers for which I have a wealth of material prepared.<br /> <br /> A ghost from Danvers possessed her in order to escape servitude. After going home one night it killed her in the hopes that it would not travel back with her to work (Danvers). What do you think might happen to the ghost afterwards? Would it snap back to its anchor at Danvers anyway? What other possibilities could there be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Might have been able to anchor itself to whatever killed her, or an object nearby. Maybe just the location. If the Ghost had Fetter as a Manifestation, it could have hitched a ride on nearly anything.<br /> <br /> Or while it was Possessing her, it could have swiped its Anchor (if it was portable, enough). In which case, it might be body-hopping still. Make the Anchor something distinct, semi-obvious, but not entirely out of place - like an ornate locket, or a scarf - and you have an easy story hook: &quot;[sister] started acting strange, right after she found that [item]. Now, someone <i>else</i> has the same [item]. Interviewing their associates uncovers that they too have started acting strange. Historical investigation reveals that the prior owner of the [item] <i>also</i> commited suicide.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T15:14:51-08:00","id":1186434,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the scarf. I'm thinking she found the scarf in one of the rooms in the Asylum not on the tour. It's a ghost's anchor as it was used for suicide by one of the Tremeres' soulless victims.<br /> <br /> The ghost compels the sister to take the scarf and then end her own life with it as well at her own apartment. Whoever finds her body is compelled to take the scarf and so on....<br /> <br /> I like it particularly because it leads eventually back to the Asylum and the Tremere are ultimately responsible for the suicides. Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T15:31:51-08:00","id":1186439,"title":"","content":"Here's the next Aspiration I'm working on:<br /> <br /> The same character has a Grimoire in his possession that has some Death Rotes he has/is learning. I've decided that the Grimoire comes from the Obsidian Palace (from Gloria Mundi Chronicle).<br /> <br /> It was stolen by an Apostate thief who was tracked down and punished by Stygian assassins. My Moros player found it somewhere.<br /> <br /> My questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Where might he have found it?<br /> 2. How and Why did the Stygian assassins kill the thief, but not manage to recover the Grimoire to return it to the Palace?<br /> 3. What would be a good way to get the Moros and his cabal to the Obsidian Palace to experience the trials?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T16:05:57-08:00","id":1186457,"title":"","content":"It's too late for me to look into the Gloria Mundi Chronicle, so my ideas might easily be off the mark.<br /> <br /> The Apostate had cast a Veiling Spell on the Grimoire that the assassins didn't manage to pierce. However, his death caused the Spell to be unsafely relinquished. After a while it begun to go haywire and your Moros found it by following the trail of strangeness. The Grimoire will still have Sympathetic links to the Palace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T17:45:02-08:00","id":1186491,"title":"","content":"2) Stygian assassins implies to me a Supernal entity, maybe generated as part of the traps in the Obsidian Palace, it managed to track down the thief and kill him, but ran out of time before returning to its circle. This would give you a chance to tie in the Abyss if you wanted.<br /> <br /> 1) In a last ditch effort the Supernal entity managed to drop the grimoire in a place it would likely be found by a Moros. It also did...something to the grimoire, binding a part of its existence to it before being snatched away or devoured by the Abyss (Similar to the Nemean leaving his heart outside the door to the Old Man by the Ocean). It either worked or it didn't, but properly investigated the grimoire might call out the Supernal entity or some Abyssal reflection of itself either to be sent back home more or less in one piece or to be contended with as it seeks to further corrupt reality.<br /> <br /> 3) The entity one way or another drops &quot;hints&quot; as to its origins in the Obsidian Palace implying, depending on what it is now, a source of greater knowledge, how it can be returned home, or a way to permanently destroy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T14:15:00-08:00","id":1186817,"title":"","content":"I like these ideas. I'll probably marry them together.<br /> <br /> Apostate thief cast a Veiling spell on the Grimoire that the Stygian assassin could not pierce (after killing the thief) before it ran out of time and was drawn into the Abyss after marking the Grimoire with part of its existence so that it could be re-summoned via a Grimoire ritual which requires the summoner to be in the Obsidian Palace. Of course, now that the entity has spent time in the Abyss it is warped in some way if it is brought back. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> After the thief's termination the unsafely relinquished veiling spell went haywire and was found by the Moros by following the trail of strangeness.<br /> <br /> So my follow up questions:<br /> <br /> 1. What is the Stygian Assassin?<br /> 2. How was it warped by the Abyss?<br /> 3. What do you think should be involved in the ritual at the Obsidian Palace to bring it back?<br /> 4. What's a good way of the Grimoire leading to the Obsidian Palace without being too obvious about it?<br /> <br /> Thanks again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T15:55:42-08:00","id":1186857,"title":"","content":"1. The Stygian Assassins role is to kill those who cross certain lines. I wouldn't make those lines ethical, because I like to treat the Supernal as amoral. It might be something esoteric like defying the cycle of life and death or, to take a cue from the Aeon of Death, trying to regain knowledge from the Time Before. The Apostate has somehow earned the Assassin's attention.<br /> <br /> 2. Having been corrupted, the Assassin desperately seeks to reaffirm its identity. To that end it tries to entrap others into breaking its rules, so it can follow its nature by killing them. This of course defeats its entire purpose as keeper of order. The Assassin also postpones the kill for as long as possible so it can take time loathing its targets. It paradoxically appreciates them for letting it hate them.<br /> <br /> Alternately it might try to change the world to undo itself. If all knowledge from the Time Before is recovered, or cycle of life and death is utterly destroyed, then its purpose is negated and it's free from itself - whatever that means. It might struggle against its original programming to kill, making it erratic and unpredictable.<br /> <br /> As for appearance, originally equipped with metal blades, they have now liquefied. Instead of cutting, the entity will drown you with metal. Its formerly rotting heart now takes a tortured semblance of life, pumping pus and maggots.<br /> <br /> 3. The Assassins corruption might have made the original ritual unusable, but if the Grimoire is still in sync with the entity, the book will be vital for the summoning. Perhaps doing the ritual properly has no effect, but making a mistake allows the Assassin to return.<br /> <br /> 4. The obvious answers are Postcognition and Scrying. If this is too easy, consider that the Obsidian Palace if a fragment of the Time Before, so it can confuse the reading, necessitating further investigation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T14:20:55-08:00","id":1187350,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> <br /> I thought you might want to know how the search for the Jade Pendant was progressing.<br /> <br /> After figuring out that the Jade Pendant was purchased by a high society french speaking woman, the Moros PI character decided to call his Contacts to see if they might have any information on someone matching her description given in vivid detail by the pawn shop owner under the influence of Perfect Recall.<br /> <br /> Maggie Yang (blogger on the unusual) told him that from her attire she seemed more Quebecois than French. Brenda (also under the influence of Perfect Recall), the Sleepwalker bartender at the Emerald Scroll said that a woman with a heavy french accent had been in a couple weeks ago with a well dressed man. He remembered that his name was Zechariah Crowther from his credit card. [I decided to let Zee be discovered through the Emerald Scroll as it might have been somewhere out of the way that he may have had meetings with Scelesti members of the Red Word from time to time - it was a bit of an easy trail, but I wanted to keep the story moving]<br /> <br /> They did some Internet research to find his apartment. At 2 o'clock in the afternoon he was at work. The Obrimos used Control Electricity to get past the door security and they made their way to his 8th floor apartment. The Obrimos used Web of Life to find one human life behind the door. The Moros used Ectoplasm to shape a key to open the lock. They tried to call out to the human presence but received no response. The Obrimos (Vice is Hasty) barged in expecting to see someone. They were both surprised when Daddy (human transformed into a Temple Hound by the Hunger) lept to attack them from behind a sofa. The Obrimos side-stepped the attack and then cast Control Gravity to keep the creature suspended in mid-air.<br /> <br /> The Moros tried to intimidate the beast into giving up information but failed dramatically. It let out a blood curdling howl which triggered the Moros Spooked Condition and he was reminded of Agartha's devouring by The Shinje. This caused him to onload his pistol into the beast, filling its track with Lethal. In a fit of fear and rage he finished the beast with Devour the Slain and failed the Wisdom roll that ensued.<br /> <br /> Realizing that the other people in the building (known through the earlier Web of Life) would call the police regarding the hail of gunfire, they took a few minutes to quickly investigate the scene. The Obrimos found the cannibal cook book (Having Friends for Dinner) and a picture of Zee with his sister Annie. He found cannibalistic resonance with Mage Sight and the hidden freezer with several flayed humans hanging in it. The Moros used a Matter spell to find the gun casings and gather them up and cast Icognito Presence on himself. The Obrimos used Mutable Mask and they made their way out.<br /> <br /> Upon exiting the elevator they ran into Annie returning from grocery shopping. The Moros sent a telepathic messsage to her as the elevator doors were closing on her: &quot;If you want answers, come to the Emerald Scroll at 8 o'clock&quot;. They quickly made their getaway.<br /> <br /> My question: What do you think Zee and Annie's response should be after they discover the open freezer, book missing and Daddy's corpse in a pool of blood?<br /> <br /> I can involve Wendigo (a Thyrsus) from Waltman's Neck or any number of Red Word cultists. I feel that Zee wouldn't be stupid enough to just march into the Emerald Scroll and start a fight, given the number of Mages or other supernaturals that might be around at 8 pm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 02-18-2018, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T16:14:19-08:00","id":1187375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.