. The Obrimos side-stepped the attack and then cast Control Gravity to keep the creature suspended in mid-air.<br /> <br /> The Moros tried to intimidate the beast into giving up information but failed dramatically. It let out a blood curdling howl which triggered the Moros Spooked Condition and he was reminded of Agartha's devouring by The Shinje. This caused him to onload his pistol into the beast, filling its track with Lethal. In a fit of fear and rage he finished the beast with Devour the Slain and failed the Wisdom roll that ensued.<br /> <br /> Realizing that the other people in the building (known through the earlier Web of Life) would call the police regarding the hail of gunfire, they took a few minutes to quickly investigate the scene. The Obrimos found the cannibal cook book (Having Friends for Dinner) and a picture of Zee with his sister Annie. He found cannibalistic resonance with Mage Sight and the hidden freezer with several flayed humans hanging in it. The Moros used a Matter spell to find the gun casings and gather them up and cast Icognito Presence on himself. The Obrimos used Mutable Mask and they made their way out.<br /> <br /> Upon exiting the elevator they ran into Annie returning from grocery shopping. The Moros sent a telepathic messsage to her as the elevator doors were closing on her: &quot;If you want answers, come to the Emerald Scroll at 8 o'clock&quot;. They quickly made their getaway.<br /> <br /> My question: What do you think Zee and Annie's response should be after they discover the open freezer, book missing and Daddy's corpse in a pool of blood?<br /> <br /> I can involve Wendigo (a Thyrsus) from Waltman's Neck or any number of Red Word cultists. I feel that Zee wouldn't be stupid enough to just march into the Emerald Scroll and start a fight, given the number of Mages or other supernaturals that might be around at 8 pm.</div> </div> </div> </div>They threw magic around - remember that that can leave traces, both to conventional scrying (I didn't see any Time Shielding spell used) and by imposing their Nimbus on things. The book might have a tracking spell on it. Did they check for Ephemerals watching from Twilight? They grabbed the bullet casings, but did they bump into anything and leave clothing fibers or skin cells?<br /> <br /> If they can identify who did it, they might seek their own leverage before the 8 pm deadline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T02:05:23-08:00","id":1187493,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the summary!<br /> <br /> Consider that the siblings must now do damage control concerning the coming police and all the evidence in their house. If they're out of luck, they might even have to leave their lives behind and find shelter among other cultists. That's unlikely to put them in a good mood, to say nothing of seeing their father shot to death.<br /> <br /> I assume they will search for whatever assistance they can get, including magic. On the other hand, they might feel this is too personal to involve help. If you want to keep it simple, have them force a proxy with a cellphone to come in their stead. The proxy's loved ones are kidnapped and held under threat of being eaten alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T08:48:39-08:00","id":1187566,"title":"","content":"Well, I've decided that Annie will be able to clean up the mess in time and get Daddy in the freezer before the police arrive without a warrant. Everyone that heard the shots was at least 3 floors down so no precise location of where the shots came from can be discerned. Thus Annie will simply open the door for the police, but not let them in. ie. I can plausibly do whatever I want and don't want them to get caught by the cops at this time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Zee and Annie are Sleeperwalker members of the Red Word. They don't have any direct magic, but have a good working relationship with some Scelesti in Waltman's Neck (Wendigo) and Howard's Rock (TBD).<br /> <br /> Thanks for your help guys. I like the idea of forcing the proxy to come instead with a cellphone. I think I'll have Wendigo park a Raven Spirit for surveillance outside that can follow them back to their Sanctum (no one in the cabal has Spirit). I'll make Zee seem agreeable on the phone to lull them into a false sense of security and then have the Raven track them.<br /> <br /> I guess ultimately I want conflict with the Red Word as a whole that might lead them to Waltman's Neck and then Howard's Rock etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T13:21:05-07:00","id":1232916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1186857#post1186857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The Stygian Assassins role is to kill those who cross certain lines. I wouldn't make those lines ethical, because I like to treat the Supernal as amoral. It might be something esoteric like defying the cycle of life and death or, to take a cue from the Aeon of Death, trying to regain knowledge from the Time Before. The Apostate has somehow earned the Assassin's attention.<br /> <br /> 2. Having been corrupted, the Assassin desperately seeks to reaffirm its identity. To that end it tries to entrap others into breaking its rules, so it can follow its nature by killing them. This of course defeats its entire purpose as keeper of order. The Assassin also postpones the kill for as long as possible so it can take time loathing its targets. It paradoxically appreciates them for letting it hate them.<br /> <br /> Alternately it might try to change the world to undo itself. If all knowledge from the Time Before is recovered, or cycle of life and death is utterly destroyed, then its purpose is negated and it's free from itself - whatever that means. It might struggle against its original programming to kill, making it erratic and unpredictable.<br /> <br /> As for appearance, originally equipped with metal blades, they have now liquefied. Instead of cutting, the entity will drown you with metal. Its formerly rotting heart now takes a tortured semblance of life, pumping pus and maggots.<br /> <br /> 3. The Assassins corruption might have made the original ritual unusable, but if the Grimoire is still in sync with the entity, the book will be vital for the summoning. Perhaps doing the ritual properly has no effect, but making a mistake allows the Assassin to return.<br /> <br /> 4. The obvious answers are Postcognition and Scrying. If this is too easy, consider that the Obsidian Palace if a fragment of the Time Before, so it can confuse the reading, necessitating further investigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm finally running this Chronicle again tonight. I don't think we will get to this particular story, but I want to be prepared.<br /> <br /> I've decided to keep the Assassin's role as simply being to hunt down and retrieve stolen items from Stygia - in this case the Grimoire stolen from the Obsidian Palace. I like the idea that it marked the Grimoire as it was running out of time and chose to leave it there as it knew it would be drawn into the Abyss and didn't want the Grimoire to end up there with it. This marking will allow a Moros Mage to re-summon it from the Abyss in an appropriate place like the Obsidian Palace.<br /> <br /> Given this, does anyone have ideas about what the original Hunter/Assassin might have looked like before and after being corrupted by the Abyss? What do you think a summoning ritual might entail?<br /> <br /> Thanks again for your help, fellow STs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T12:40:27-07:00","id":1233247,"title":"","content":"Our options are varied and many. Did you consider which Arcanum to tie Supernal Assassins to, beyond Death? Such beings tend to have two, and you can tailor the other to fit your players. That would help narrow the symbolism down and suggest a distinctive thing it can do. Among things that can kill you suddenly or without you noticing:<br /> <br /> (Death/Life or Spirit) Predators. Hounds in particular are often associated with death and doom (Fate), and are capable of pursuit (Space), killing and retrieval.<br /> (Death/Life, Matter or Space) Spiders can use traps (Space) and poison (Matter), come in a variety of sizes and may wrap reclaimed goods in cocoons.<br /> (Death/Life) Plague victims or plague carrying animals, from rats to mosquitoes. You can remove the middleman and use a miasma of disease.<br /> (Death/Matter) Machines including, but not limited to, T-1000 from Terminator 2 or a disembodied intelligence possessing electrical devices (Killdozer).<br /> (Death/Fate) Some discarnate thing that manifests through coincidences and events, like in the Final Destination series.<br /> (Death/Forces) A display of eerie lights, killing you with heat or radiation. You can make an attack seem like an alien visitation.<br /> (Death/???) A modern image of a hit-man has a feature of being subtle, but also showing that the Supernal isn't outdated.<br /> (Death/Spirit) <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k2R07EbLjSU\" target=\"_blank\">For something more ephemeral you can borrow from this eerie scene.</a><br /> (Death/???) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show#post793173\">This guy.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T15:27:37-07:00","id":1233288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1233247#post1233247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Death/<b>Mind</b>) A modern image of a hit-man has a feature of being subtle, but also showing that the Supernal isn't outdated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have it make liberal use of the Imposter (Mind 3) Spell, when it isn't simply running Incognito Presence (Mind 2) to get close to targets. Wrap everything up nicely with a No Witnesses bow, by using Memory Hole (Mind 2).<br /> <br /> Death/Prime - Eidolon of the Perfect Assassin, or Words Of Death that make the target <i>know</i> they will/should die.<br /> Death/Time - Erases the target from existence, like A Wonderful Life, except the target/victim doesn't get to go back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-09-2018, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T14:52:33-07:00","id":1233519,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the ideas. I'll come back to the Grimoire at some point, but I thought I'd give everyone an update on how it went.<br /> <br /> I had the Red Word kidnap (after school) the daughter of someone who works in the same building as Zee to force him to be the go-between at the Emerald Scroll.<br /> <br /> Before the meeting, the PCs headed back to the pawn shop to see if the French woman was the one in the photo (no - actually Annie Crowther, Zee's cannibal sister). They did find out that the French woman walked in and specifically described and asked for the Jade Pendant. They headed to the Emerald Scroll after that around 7:30 PM.<br /> <br /> The father showed up and was quite nervous, just trying to get everything over with. He handed a burner phone to the Moros PC (who uses Mind like crazy and probably should have been a Mastigos, LOL) and Zee called and demanded an explanation for the mess in his apartment. The Moros was fairly belligerent and demanded that Zee produce the French woman who purchased the Pendant. Zee indicated that she was out of town, but that he would call him on the burner phone when a meeting was possible. Zee indicated that the father could go home and that his daughter was fine back at his apartment.<br /> <br /> The Moros got it in his head that he really wanted to protect this father &amp; daughter and the only way to do that would be to escort them back to his apartment. He was hoping to confront the Red Word, but I decided they weren't stupid enough to fight them on short notice. The PCs were followed by a Raven spirit, undetectable as no one in the cabal has spirit.<br /> <br /> They discovered that the daughter was safe and reunited her with her father. They just wanted to be left alone, but The Moros was insistent (Emotional Urging, passed Wisdom check) that they stay a couple nights in The Loft (Cabal's Sanctum) for safety reasons. The father agreed (due to Emotional Urging) and they packed and left. We ended there.<br /> <br /> So, I figure that Zee and Annie and the rest of the Red Word want to dispense with the cabal, but aren't dumb enough to think they can do it without help. I was thinking of using Wendigo indirectly, by sending some kind of Spirit to help the Red Word attack them when the moment is right. My questions:<br /> <br /> 1. What would Wendigo send? He's no slouch (Fate 4, Life 4, Spirit 4, Prime 3).<br /> 2. When and where do you think the Red Word would attack?<br /> <br /> Really appreciate the help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T05:40:55-07:00","id":1233661,"title":"","content":"1. I would let Wendigo empower the cultists with magic, preferably through sending them a temporary Imbued Item. Permanent Imbued Items require Prime 4, but Prime 3 might be enough for our purposes. We can also assume he had one laying around. You have a chance to add a neat visual. The Spell can be activated by smearing ash over the cultists, or carving sigils into their skin. Deactivating it could require washing off the ash, or healing the injuries with magic. Suggested Spells, and you can bundle multiple ones into one effect, include:<br /> <br /> Exceptional Luck (Fate 2)<br /> Warding Gesture (Fate 2)<br /> Honing the Form (Life 3)<br /> Transform Life (Life 3)<br /> Wards and Signs (Prime 2)<br /> <br /> I don't know how much of a challenge each Spirit would pose for your players, so you need to make that decision. I assume Wendigo will work with what he knows (classic Mage tunnel vision) and send an unpleasant nature spirit. Maybe even a Gulmoth, if you're not worried by revealing the Abyssal connection too early:<br /> <br /> Command Spirit (Spirit 2)<br /> Bolster Spirit (Spirit 3)<br /> World Walker (Spirit 4)<br /> <br /> In addition:<br /> <br /> Many Faces (Life 3) can be used to disguise a cultist as someone under the PCs' protection.<br /> Ephemeral Enchantment (Prime 3) can make a Spirit able to use material weapons. Without Spirit Arcanum your PC need to disable the weapon or turn it against the user.<br /> <br /> The Cult themselves are no strangers to kidnapping people. They must have some basic tactics and equipment they feel comfortable using. Above that, they can get Sleeper witnesses to provoke Paradox, and suffer from your PCs' careless casting. That last tactic requires some minor adjustments. Any Spirit Wendigo sends over must be capable of Manifesting and willing to cause havoc without magical coercion. Enhancements they Cultists get should likewise be on the subtle side.<br /> <br /> 2. If they're smart they won't attack Mages while they're in their Sanctum. They will try to lure your characters out. They can do this through offers of parley, or by using the Moros' attachment against him and kidnapping the mother of their protected family, or letting Wendigo use Fate to have them run into one another. Wendigo of all people should know you don't give Mages time to prepare, so the attack could come as soon as convenient. They can also send people to ransack the Sanctum while the Cabal is occupied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 07-10-2018, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T08:11:03-07:00","id":1233704,"title":"","content":"Seeing as Imbued Items are off the table (baring homebrew or hacks), Spirit 4 has Craft Fetish - give the cultists a few Fetishes with useful Influences or Numina. If you want to be nasty, there was that Countermagic Numen from 1E's Astral Realms you might convert (or was that done in Dark Eras?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T08:18:32-07:00","id":1233707,"title":"","content":"Cultists are probably fairly easy to convince that Possession is a good thing, letting a portion of their god ride in them or whatever lie you want to come up with. The advantage is that when a spirit Possesses someone it can spend Essence to heal Lethal damage on a one for one basis which effectively turns them into Wolverine. They also are much more difficult to control with Mind or Life since the Spirit can impose a CoW before any such spell can set in. If the Spirit stops Possessing a cultist, and still has Essence, it can become another combatant and regains access to its Numina and Influences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-10-2018, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T13:29:41-07:00","id":1234381,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Really great suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T15:13:56-07:00","id":1255595,"title":"","content":"We played another 4 sessions and I thought I'd share an update:<br /> <br /> The PCs decided to track the Red Word's &quot;HQ&quot; via the kidnapped little girl's Perfect Recall of her brief abduction. They narrowed things down to a 5 block area and the Obrimos Perfected Adept in the cabal used Web of Life to find unusual clusters of people in the area. He found an unusually large number of people gathered in the basement of a Coptic church in the Back Bay area of Boston.<br /> <br /> Infiltrating the church led them to Zee, Annie and 4 other cultists about to perform a human ritual sacrifice and cannibalism ritual on a middle-aged woman strapped to a large table.<br /> <br /> I took some of the suggestions here and all of these cultists had increased Stamina via Honing the Form and a Potency 4 Wards and Signs. Half of them had guns and the other half had melee weapons.<br /> <br /> I expected this to be a tough fight for two Disciples, but the Moros surprised me by Shaping Shadows to plunge the room into complete darkness instead of targeting the cultists directly, while the Obrimos gave both PCs Nightvision. Then the Moros improvised a Weaving spell with area scale we called Shadow Binding that created a solid blanket of shadow that entangled most of the cultists for half the fight, while the Obrimos unleashed multiple Telekinetic Strikes to devastating effect [since the earlier spells had been immune from the effects of Wards and Signs I actually forgot to subtract their potency from the TK, but honestly it would not have mattered much to the outcome of the fight as the Obrimos likely would have simply entered melee with his devastating Subak instead.]<br /> <br /> It didn't take long for the cult to realize they needed to retreat, so the leader held up a fetish [open mandible child's skull] that activated a Gateway into Shadow and they retreated, except for Zee who was still trapped under the shadow blanket.<br /> <br /> They rescued the woman and called Maggie Yang (reporter contact) to come and help get her to safety and the Moros promised to give her the exclusive if she helped the woman get to a hospital while they take Zee for interrogation.<br /> <br /> With the help of Elegua (Special Media Group) after agreeing to a mutual defense pact between their cabals, they managed to learn about the Cult and their worship of the Prince, but not the nature of the Prince. The Mastigos PC that plays sporadically went with the Obrimos to Zee's apartment to retrieve his computer. There they briefly fought some cultists and drove them off and managed to retrieve Zee's partially erased unusable computer.<br /> <br /> They Psychic Programmed Zee to turn himself into the BPD and identify some of his fellow cultists and admit to his crimes and gave him a Memory Hole regarding the Cabal.<br /> <br /> After getting back to The Loft (Sanctum), the Obrimos reconstructed the computer's OS with a Forces Perfecting Spell and managed to retrieve 3 Fragments of the Prince, his mother's address in Waltman's Neck (coastal fishing village), and some emails from Wendigo about a Summer Solstice feast soon to be held at Waltman's Inn.<br /> <br /> They didn't immediately take the bait and decided to research Khonsu Tohut (The Prince) more. They found one of the 3 Fragments in a book published by the publishing house that Zee edits for. By looking through the other published books they managed to find 8 more Fragments. With the help of Adgos (Brotherhood of Ineffable Truth) they figured out that the Fragments tell some kind of story that reads like The Bible. The found out many names for the Prince, but still have no clue as to its true nature.<br /> <br /> A day after Zee turned himself in, they got a call from Maggie Yang that he disappeared from his cell. The cabal figured he was rescued by cultists using the Gateway Fetish (and they're right).<br /> <br /> They finally decided to go to Waltman's neck to investigate Waltman's Inn. They were constantly followed by Raven spirits loyal to Wendigo, but no one in the cabal has Spirit so they just get the occasional PMS ping that is annoying them.<br /> <br /> They met Jules Bagron and ate a hardy lunch at the Inn and he spiked their beer with a sedative. Having had more than everyone else, the Moros fell asleep unexpectedly in their room after lunch. The Obrimos suspected foul play and prepared to cast Cleanse the Body on the cabal when the session ended ....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 09-19-2018, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T01:10:23-07:00","id":1255675,"title":"","content":"Aah... I missed this. All around this sounds like a fine session. As for the battle, I think our collective advice assumed the cultists would be performing the first strike. If they were surprised on their turf, they'd probably be lacking protective spells, but the area itself would be Signed and Warded. That would have prevented your Moros' instant victory. Still, if the players had fun that's all that matters.<br /> <br /> How many Fragments do they have to gather before things get &quot;strange&quot; for them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 09-20-2018, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T10:34:29-07:00","id":1255802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1255675#post1255675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aah... I missed this. All around this sounds like a fine session. As for the battle, I think our collective advice assumed the cultists would be performing the first strike. If they were surprised on their turf, they'd probably be lacking protective spells, but the area itself would be Signed and Warded. That would have prevented your Moros' instant victory. Still, if the players had fun that's all that matters.<br /> <br /> How many Fragments do they have to gather before things get &quot;strange&quot; for them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From my understanding, the fragments are already written down and known to at least one person, so the changes caused by them are already in play. In order for things to get stranger, new fragments would need to be transcribed. <br /> <br /> I'll be paying attention to this thread as I'm intrigued by what's happened so far. I tried running a Boston campaign with the Prince as the antagonist but it died about 5 sessions in, so I'm really interested in seeing how a party handles dealing with such a foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T13:58:55-07:00","id":1255874,"title":"","content":"I'm happy with the way things turned out. Capturing Zee allowed the interrogation that revealed the information that moved the story forward.<br /> <br /> On a side note, the PCs have each received exactly 88 total beats (reg + a) in 11 sessions. So 8 per session. The Moros is G3 Death 3 Mind 2 Matter 1 and the Obrimos is G2 Forces 3 Life 3 Prime 2.<br /> <br /> Tengu: Officially you need to use the Fragments while performing a ritual or spell to make the History of those Fragments a reality after you combine them.<br /> <br /> So here's where I could use some advice.<br /> <br /> I'm planning the end game to be some kind of battle in Howard's Rock near the Temple of Holy Devouring, to stop the ritual by Red Word Mages that would combine enough Fragments to make Rhukavira the true history of Boston. At least two Mages (Wendigo and the Red King), a big Gulmoth, the Emerald Guard (royal cannibal spirits from the anti-history), Chenoo (native cannibal spirits), and a ton of Red Word cultists. It's probably too much for two PCs, although the Mastigos will likely be there as well (only has 14 beats so far though). They'll likely recruit help from Arrow and Free Council allies.<br /> <br /> Working backward, I think a battle in Waltman's Neck against Wendigo in his Cave Sanctum where he escapes into Shadow would be pretty cool. This would be after his attempt to have Jules Bagron and some cultists take out the cabal in their sleep (which they've already seen through) fails.<br /> <br /> Wendigo is fairly powerful Gnosis 4, Fate 4, Life 4, Spirit 4, Prime 3 Mage.<br /> <br /> So starting with the attack at the inn: <br /> <br /> I'll likely have the cultists buffed with various spells. I might also have Wards and Signs on Waltman's Inn as well. [I take it that Warding Gesture could make the buffs on the cultists immune to the area Wards and Signs?]. The simple thing would be to have the same group of cultists that they fought last time come at them again, but better prepared.<br /> <br /> If they go after Wendigo in his sanctum I'd like there to be some serious stuff to contend with. Do any of you have suggestions based on his capabilities? Bear in mind that none of the PCs have Spirit, but that the Moros has a pistol with a permanent Ephemeral Enchantment on it. I'm expecting them to attack the sanctum with the Mastigos PC (Space 3, Mind 2, Fate 1) and Agdos from the Brotherhood of Ineffable Truth (Gnosis 2, Matter 3) helping out.<br /> <br /> Once again, I appreciate the help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T15:10:35-07:00","id":1255913,"title":"","content":"It's pretty late where I'm writing from, so my post is rather rudimentary:<br /> <br /> 1. I'm surprised that Chenoo are working with the Cult. According to the books, they view the Emerald Guard as invaders and competition. That doesn't mean you can't change things. It's merely something that stood out to me.<br /> <br /> 2. I think Wards and Signs affects spells only as they're cast, so it won't do anything to preexisting spells. At some point in the past I wrote a post on combining Fate and Prime for the purpose of fighting, that you might find it useful.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980165-%E2%80%8B-2e-fight-fire-with-fire-running-awakened-antagonists?p=980306#post980306\">Link</a><br /> <br /> 3. Before you design Wendigo's Sanctum, ask your players how they're planning to proceed. It would be a shame to prepare an amazing fight just to have your players stealth their way in with explosives, or reroute a river to wash everything away, or otherwise skip the encounter. Once they tell you what they want, you can plan accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T09:38:33-07:00","id":1256128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1255874#post1255874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tengu: Officially you need to use the Fragments while performing a ritual or spell to make the History of those Fragments a reality after you combine them.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I must have forgotten about that part. Or missed it. Been a while since I looked at the Red Word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T09:44:21-07:00","id":1256130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1255913#post1255913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Before you design Wendigo's Sanctum, ask your players how they're planning to proceed. It would be a shame to prepare an amazing fight just to have your players stealth their way in with explosives, or reroute a river to wash everything away, or otherwise skip the encounter. Once they tell you what they want, you can plan accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally love it when my players come up with ludicrously overpowered but realistic solutions to problems. But yes, if they have something up their sleeve that will simply bypass the encounter, best to know about it so you can plan around it (or just not plan if you don't need to).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T10:45:36-07:00","id":1256154,"title":"","content":"1. What I've decided so far is that Wendigo has promised a place for the Chenoo in the new reality and so far they believe him. The characters could exploit this to turn the Chenoo against the Red Word if they clued into it. Their research has revealed the Chenoo vs. Emerald Guard divide, but I'm not sure they're going to put it all together. It also gives me the chance to have the Chenoo turn on the cult if the PCs need help at some point.<br /> <br /> 2. Yes. That makes sense. I was incorrectly thinking of Wards and Signs as an anti-magic zone, but it's just Withstand against new spells cast. My mistake. Thanks for the link. Very useful.<br /> <br /> 3. Good idea, but I'd like to have something default prepared anyway. In particular I'm trying to figure out how a Mage stated like Wendigo would likely protect his sanctum. In other words, if you were playing him, what would you do as a PC to protect yourself?<br /> <br /> Btw, the way Sanctum works in my game is that it's extra spell control slots for Sanctum buffing spells. I think I would be fine with Wendigo having Sanctum 3 and thus 3 additional spells not taking active spell slots. Then I could see two other situational spells before the fight happens so that he still has two slots available during the fight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 10-22-2018, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T11:02:57-07:00","id":1256165,"title":"","content":"Rouse Spirit on the Sanctum would probably be one of the biggest possible defense measures he could take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T12:33:51-07:00","id":1256196,"title":"","content":"Just looking quickly at Life, if a known attack is imminent, Shapechanging (4) yourself or a minion could provide an edge. And Many Faces (3) could be used to create a lookalike decoy to divert attention briefly. <br /> <br /> Chaos Master (Fate 4) combined with some traps, random dangerous obstacles etc could be useful. Think Home Alone with the traps being powered by Fate magic (Yes of course it makes sense that the falling object landed perfectly on his head and didn't just bounce harmlessly off his shoulder or something). <br /> <br /> I'm at work so my ability to think creatively on this is limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T13:40:18-07:00","id":1256212,"title":"","content":"The Spirit Arcanum is Wendigo\u2019s major asset. Him not using it would be contrived, especially since you\u2019ve established that Chenoo help him. However, if you\u2019re worried that the PCs won\u2019t be able to handle them note the following:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>Gossamer Touch (Prime 2) will let Mages strike against Spirits, even if they remain invisible. Such a fight would force players to be creative.<br /> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>Although the Mages can\u2019t see Spirits, Spirits can see them. If the PCs present evidence of Wendigo\u2019s duplicity, they can convince the Chenoo to stand back, or even to help.<br /> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>There can be a Verge within the Sanctum leading to a specifically \u201ccultivated\u201d area of the Shadow. The PCs would be in unfamiliar territory, but could actually see their opponents. You could also show how Wendigo\u2019s practices affected the Shadow. On that note, you can start with something subtle on the Material side. I recommend reading this: <a href=\"http://goblinpunch.blogspot.com/2014/09/the-devil-in-north-woods.html\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>Seriously, read this\u2026<br /> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>Read it!<br /> <br /> As for oddities and tactics within the Sanctum:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>Let\u2019s assume that Wendigo can create one-shot Imbued Items (Prime 3) and used it to leave traps. Touching the wrong thing can activate any of the spells Wendigo knows.<br /> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>\u201cDamned if you do, damned if you don\u2019t\u201d scenarios. There may be traps, trials and gateways that can be safely interacted with only by cannibals. At the same time there may be effects that make cannibals especially vulnerable. The characters can choose to take a sip of each others blood to proceed, but what happens if the slip into a Left-Handed vision quest?<br /> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>In fact, if you make Wendigo\u2019s Sanctum into a sort of training gauntlet for the Cult, you can excuse many Dungeon-crawly elements. There can be still-bleeding messages cut into hides of live animals, or forming from writhing maggots, or heard in a drug-induced haze \u2013 all clues or lessons for supplicants.<br /> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>If Wendigo adopted the Jade Pendant Legacy, he might be trying to transform a captive materialized Spirit \u2013 something the prisoner is unhappy about. Will the PCs free the Spirit or will they be discouraged by its obvious mutations?<br /> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>The Sanctum may be guarded by Claimed animals, people or objects. The second option may prompt the PCs to disable the enemy for further exorcism, instead of hurting them. The third option gives you a neat visual of animate sculptures, hedge-animals (like in the Shining) or plastic flamingos.<br /> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>You can place Fetishes laying around \u2013 ready to be send to the Cultists with instruction manuals. The PCs know how to use them, but don\u2019t know what Spirits are trapped within and what the side-effects might be.<br /> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>Also, whatever tactic The Red Word Cult could use, Wendigo can do too. You can refresh your memory on that old post: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1233661#post1233661\">Link</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T10:55:09-07:00","id":1256512,"title":"","content":"All fantastic suggestions everyone! Thanks. I'll let you know how it develops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T20:27:40-07:00","id":1262284,"title":"","content":"So both my games have had sessions since my last post. I'll probably give more details later, but I thought I would share how the attempt by the enhanced Red Word cultists to take out the cabal went.<br /> <br /> The session started with Wards and Signs 5 falling over the Inn. This never really mattered for the fight. For some reason the PCs just completely changed tactics and didn't try any AoE spells, even though they didn't know the Inn was protected. The ping to their PMS did put them on alert though. They thought about trying to leave by the window, but the gathering storm coming in off the Atlantic changed their minds. They thought it was part of the attack, but it was merely there to set the mood.<br /> <br /> The Obrimos used Web of Life and realized that a group of humans were making their way upstairs to them. He waited until they were in sight on the landing coming up the stairs to attempt dispellation of their personal Wards and Signs 4, but he failed.<br /> <br /> The Moros was determined to end the fight against the cultists (all Sleepwalkers, btw) decisively by attempting Ghost Gate on all of them. In our game it's Withstood by Stamina if targeted explicitly. The cultists were buffed with Honing the Form and all had Stamina 5, which when combined with W&amp;S gave them Withstands of 6. The Moros assumed that 6 Potency would do it and the spell failed. He had Gnosis 3 + Death 3 + WP 3 + 1 Tool = 10 dice -6 for +3 Potency =4. He used his free Reach for instant, then +1 to target them directly, +1 Sensory, + 1 switch Primary, + 1 for A-Duration and +1 for 5 targets. I was surprised to see the Paradox Pool hit 10 - 2 Dedicated tool - 3 Mana spent = 5 dice. He ended up with 2 R-Bashing after containing what I rolled. It was a Scene-ending spell and I was impressed he could possibly pull it off, even though it fizzled due to Withstand considerations.<br /> <br /> They fired a round of shots at the cabal to varying degrees of success and then Agdos turned their guns into liquid metal. They tried again with melee weapons and a full charge, but she did the same State Change again rendering their weapons useless, so they ran, but not before 3 Chenoo materialized to attack with their talons.<br /> <br /> The Obrimos cast Kinetic Blow and started tearing through the cannibal spirits like butter, but they were enough of a distraction that the Red Word escaped.<br /> <br /> It was a fun fight, but I learned that Sleepwalkers, even buffed and armed to the teeth were not a much challenge for 3 Mages. On the other hand, I learned that Paradox could be a thing at Gnosis 3+ if they aren't careful, particularly as combat gets into later rounds.<br /> <br /> I'm still prepping for the big confrontation at Wendigo's Sanctum with a lot of the ideas in this thread. I'll let you know how it goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T01:50:19-07:00","id":1262318,"title":"","content":"I'm not 100% certain, but I think &quot;Wards and Signs&quot; over the Inn should have prevented &quot;State Change&quot; from working (maybe &quot;Kinetic Blow&quot; as well). AoE Spells affect all valid targets within their sphere of influence, for as long as they stay within that sphere of influence. This means that to stand a chance against the Cultists, the PCs would have needed to figure out what's going on and lure them out of the Inn. Considering that they didn't, it might have been a good idea to ignore that Spell anyway, so it all turned for the best. It could have been brutal otherwise.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, who cast the AoE Spell? Did they have Awakened support on the scene?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T06:26:15-07:00","id":1262348,"title":"","content":"In my head I just said that Wendigo cast the spell from up the hill or something, but you've convinced me that it would have stopped the other spells so I'm going to retcon it that it was just some kind of Web of Life spell to see where the cabal was. They never figured out what the spell was anyway. I'll save the AoE W&amp;S for the next fight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T07:45:14-07:00","id":1262356,"title":"","content":"Make sure to give your players a fighting chance, or at least a forewarning! No-selling their magic would be really nasty as a surprise.<br /> <br /> Until then, I appreciate the updates. I'm eager to know how your youngest group is doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T13:41:10-07:00","id":1262403,"title":"","content":"The other Boston group had an interesting session, also focused on combat. The kids seemed to like it. I usually do a session recap for that group, so I'll post it here when I have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T10:19:39-07:00","id":1264446,"title":"","content":"So I like the suggestion in the other thread where a Fate 4 mage can create a Chaos Mastery field in his sanctum that he is immune to through Warding Gesture.<br /> <br /> In this vein, I've decided to have this in place in the cave portion of Wendigo's sanctum with a Potency of 6. The way I picture this cave is a narrow crack in the basement that eventually widens into a corridor, which leads to a larger cavern no longer under the house. Wendigo's summoning circle is in one part of the cavern. His library is in another part. The cave could have an exit in the cliff side overlooking the Atlantic, but there has to be a practical way to keep the elements out of the cave since it is a library/sanctum.<br /> <br /> What cool effects and what kind of mechanics do you guys suggest for the Potency 6 Chaos Mastery. Will the Potency 6 mean 6 different events total or 6 different events to each character in the area? Or maybe 6 different events that could affect multiple intruders?<br /> <br /> Your suggestions are appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 11-03-2018, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T16:47:22-07:00","id":1264524,"title":"","content":"Considering the way AoE works, 6 total.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-04T03:10:05-08:00","id":1264578,"title":"","content":"I think whatever events you plan for the &quot;Chaos Mastery&quot;, they should feel ridiculously contrived. That would signify to your players that something is off, as opposed to thinking that you're personally messing with them. Did you ever see the &quot;Final Destination&quot; series?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=inT_CDCCi5Y\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a><br /> <br /> Without going into details, use every point of Potency on a <i>chain</i> of events ending with a threat. Employ Rube-Goldberg events. Tell your players of a potential danger, and when they try to address it, spring another danger at them and <i>then</i> have them to roll dice. An example in action: PC-1 slips on wet leaves and starts sliding towards a jagged pit. PC-2 tries to help, but steps into a hole and breaks their ankle. PC-3 tries to cast a spell, but a tool stand interrupts by falling at them in that moment. For extra humor, PC-1 gets snagged by a rock outcropping and is completely unhurt. If you want to turn the screw even further, after they figure out something is off describe every potential threat in detail - make them paranoid.<br /> <br /> You can make the cave into a workshop where Wendigo processes carcasses, makes traps and keeps Yantras. That would fill the place with jagged and noxious things to be wary of. Possible hazards include:<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 Slippery leaves make for a tripping hazard and may hide other threats.<br /> \u200b\u2022 A deep pit or well filled with human and animal bones.<br /> \u2022 Uneven footing and rock outcroppings carrying a risk of injury\u200b.<br /> \u200b\u2022 A section of the roof collapsing.<br /> \u2022 Venomous animals, like spiders or snakes.<br /> \u200b\u2022 Hidden tripwires and bear traps.<br /> \u200b\u2022 Sharp, heavy or pointy equipment.<br /> \u200b\u2022 Tool racks that can spontanously collapse.<br /> \u200b\u2022 Containers with concentrated lye (for soap).<br /> \u200b</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 Ash and granulate materials getting blown in their faces.<br /> \u200b\u2022 Breakable jars with angry hornets.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T09:46:39-08:00","id":1264750,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Any mechanical advice for the above ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T12:25:08-08:00","id":1264777,"title":"","content":"The cave contains pre-existing dangers. You can describe them to the players, or demand a perception check. Either way, if your players have time to make decisions, a threat is not part of the Spell.<br /> <br /> According to the Spell description, you should use standard rules for every hazard it causes. I'm afraid you'll have to consult the books for what options you like most. I tried to write down an algorithm of your options, but the sheer variety is killing me. To keep it simple, every time &quot;Chaos Mastery&quot; endangers a PC, they are forced to make an unexpected roll. This uses up 1 Potency of the Spell. You can reduce any of these rolls to a Chance Die using 1 extra Potency. For 1 Potency, you can also inflict Conditions on your PCs, without a roll. Best to do it as a punchline, after they successfully avoid a different threat. If something is only there to psych them out and they don't get to roll against it, no Potency is spent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T14:00:25-08:00","id":1265114,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">This is what I settled on. Please critique if you have the time:<br /> <br /> - Falling Stalactite (Dice Pool 10 - Defense, +2L)<br /> - Roof section collapse (Dex + Athletics - 5 or Immobilized Tilt)<br /> - Slippery limestone (Arm or Leg Wrack Tilt)<br /> - Insect Cloud (Full Blinded Tilt)<br /> - Deep (9 meter) well filled with human and animal bones (3B - [Dex + Athletics successes])</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Snake bite (Northern Copperhead - Chance die to avoid): 6 - (Stamina + Resolve - 6) -&gt; Lethal damage per minute</span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u200b<br /> <br /> I think this should be enough.<br /> <br /> I'm also looking for a 3rd sanctum wide spell (the other is Wards &amp; Signs). Any suggestions?</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T16:05:06-08:00","id":1265140,"title":"","content":"It's pretty late for me, so I'll be brief:<br /> <br /> Did you decide how to chain events together?<br /> <br /> Do your PCs have Life to heal themselves of damage? If not, can they use Wendigo's equipment to make splints, stretchers and antidotes?<br /> <br /> Make sure Tilts become relevant for further decision-making.<br /> <br /> As for the third Sanctum Spell, what comes to my mind is:<br /> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>Degrading the Form (Life <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022</span></span>) Rules as written - you can reduce everyone's Physical Attribute of your choice. <br /> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>Control Instincts (Life <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022) GM's call - you can bribe your players with Beats for making bad decisions.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T09:46:46-08:00","id":1265300,"title":"","content":"Yes. One of the PCs has Life 3.<br /> <br /> I'll likely figure out the chaining of events during play.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for all your suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T02:10:14-08:00","id":1283874,"title":"","content":"Looking back, the entire discussion has gone scarily elaborate. Did everything work out during play?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T14:48:27-08:00","id":1284012,"title":"","content":"I havent read the whole thread yet but, could the hallow be protected by its own Resonance? Like a sort of weak obfuscation effect that works on Sleepers?<br /> <br /> Edit: sorry didnt realize this was an older thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 01-31-2019, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T12:29:05-07:00","id":1323250,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping to get some write-ups done soon for Boston 1.0 and Boston 2.0 (which are still alive and in hiatus right now), but now I'm starting Boston 3.0 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> One of my players is playing a Moros (Matter 3, Death 2, Life 1) street performer and wants to have a Rank 2 spirit familiar - Jackalope Trickster Spirit based on Manabohzo the rabbit trickster god of Native American origin. Apparently the jackalope can be appeased by feeding it whiskey.<br /> <br /> 1) What kind of Essence should it feed on?<br /> 2) Does anyone have suggested Bans or Banes?<br /> 3) Does anyone have suggested Numina?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T13:02:19-07:00","id":1323259,"title":"","content":"One kind of Essence should be obvious, whiskey. Perhaps it feeds by being around someone who has consumed enough whiskey to suffer the Drugged Tilt, and being a trickster Spirit in order to consume that Essence it then has to play a trick on said individual. Little things like making a drunk forget where he parked his car or return to the wrong home.<br /> For Bans how about his Influence and Numina don't work on Tea Tootlers? For Banes cold water, strong coffee and an AA sticker wrapped around a baseball bat.<br /> For Numina how about Dement, Hallucination and Implant Mission (people get the strangest ideas when they're drunk).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T01:16:53-07:00","id":1323394,"title":"","content":"Sounds like the Ban is that it cannot be hostile toward anyone that has offered it whiskey for this scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T07:43:13-07:00","id":1323444,"title":"","content":"Do you think gaining Essence from tricks, deception etc... would be appropriate? I like the whiskey ban and cold water banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T09:42:04-07:00","id":1323460,"title":"","content":"Tricks and deceptions played by other people would be very appropriate, just has rage Spirits feed from people on the highway.<br /> The real question is should there be additional qualifiers, such as malicious intent or actual harm being done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T19:50:41-07:00","id":1323588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1323444#post1323444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think gaining Essence from tricks, deception etc... would be appropriate? I like the whiskey ban and cold water banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bane should be antabuse. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T20:20:20-07:00","id":1324606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1099827#post1099827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. What would be a nice way to tie in the Raven/Greed Spirit if I go with the Arcadian Verge idea?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Greed is a perfect doom for people which could emanate out from Arcadia. <br /> <br /> I was thinking about the Legacy and you could go for a Left-Handed or very militant AA one which teaches how to create and circulate cursed/doomed items to punish the greedy or enemies of Awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25371-elzopilote","name":"elzopilote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25371_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T07:30:40-07:00","id":1324730,"title":"","content":"The new cabal has their Sanctum in an old dilapidated duplex in Roxbury. What would be a good 5 point Hallow concept for this Sanctum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T10:58:29-07:00","id":1324774,"title":"","content":"What's the place's story?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T13:35:15-07:00","id":1324801,"title":"","content":"Roxbury has a strong history of crime and violence and as written in Boston Unveiled even today it resists attempts at gentrification. It is also home to Mama Desta, a Tremere Lich.<br /> It would fit that the duplex once served as a crack house and a house of prostitution, mixing the business of both.<br /> If it is a 5 dot Hallow then it will have a long history with the Awakened, or if a new Hallow something extreme must have happened here to form it.<br /> Going the former I would give it a mixed resonance of lost innocence and cannibalism. <br /> The lost innocence would be an echo of whatever resonance it once had, while the cannibalism would come first from the native Awakened using cannibal spirits against the European settlers, then in recent history by the willingness of people to use, abuse and destroy others for selfish profit or to satisfy appetites.<br /> As ST I would be inclined to give it the Addictive or Toxic negative trait, possibly both if being really mean. The Toxic would present itself as a drug related substance that can get you arrested if caught carrying it about.<br /> In the end it would be a big 'kick me' sign for the Red Word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T20:39:37-07:00","id":1324865,"title":"","content":"Your ideas are really good, but these are new to Mage players and I'd like something more positive for their 1st Hallow. I'm fine with the resonance being lost innocence (prostitution, Mama Desta's soulless children, etc...), but don't want the Tass to be drug related as the plot of my first story revolves around a mysterious drug. Any ideas for how the Hallow's tass could work with this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T13:03:46-07:00","id":1325045,"title":"","content":"Given that it is a 5 dot Hallow that no one else had claimed it should be somewhat hidden. This leaves the question of how your characters found it, did they inherit it?<br /> <br /> For a less difficult background that is still interesting how about tying it to Prohibition?<br /> Place the Hallow in a hidden cellar down in the basement where the remains of a Prohibition still, possibly even a small speak easy, lie forgotten. Any drink produced with the still, even if the alcohol content is weak, absorbs the Mana producing liquid Tass.<br /> <br /> For a small but potentially interesting mystery you could place it on an underground Ley Line that passes under the Combat Zone in China Town.<br /> <br /> If instead you just want it to be a 5 dot Hallow that only recently came into being you could instead make it a product of the 'Big Dig' that has only recently been discovered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T16:56:16-07:00","id":1325089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1324801#post1324801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lost innocence would be an echo of whatever resonance it once had, while the cannibalism would come first from the native Awakened using cannibal spirits against the European settlers, then in recent history by the willingness of people to use, abuse and destroy others for selfish profit or to satisfy appetites.</div> </div> </div> </div>I HIGHLY advice against using &quot;cannibal natives&quot; tropes because it's racist af.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T19:05:58-07:00","id":1325124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1325089#post1325089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I HIGHLY advice against using &quot;cannibal natives&quot; tropes because it's racist af.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially since the Pequot and Wampanoag and other Boston-local Algonquin-speaking first nations people had no similar traditions, but you could use echoes of the Pequot and &quot;King Phillip's&quot; war as a basis for the mysterious substance. It might be forgetting/erasure resonance from tainted ley lines distilled down into a derivative of mana refinement. The more recent historical monograph, Christine Delucia's <i>Memory Lands</i> could serve as some inspiration for examining the underbelly of settler colonialism which the Boston mages are based on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25371,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25371-elzopilote","user":"elzopilote","date":". 07-16-2019, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25371-elzopilote","name":"elzopilote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25371_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T22:57:41-07:00","id":1325157,"title":"","content":"No one said the natives were cannibals. The Boston Unveiled book tells of how native mages used cannibal spirits to attack the settlers, spirits not the natives. Then it tells of how the original Ebon Knot Cabal used a dread ritual to summon the Prince of 10,000 Leaves to rewrite history so that the natives never released those spirits against them.<br /> It was the last surviving member of that Cabal that started the Red Word, as the meal in a cannibal ritual.<br /> The native shamans were just using a violent spirit as a weapon. That is what Spirit mages do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T14:50:14-07:00","id":1325400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1325157#post1325157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one said the natives were cannibals. The Boston Unveiled book tells of how native mages used cannibal spirits to attack the settlers, spirits not the natives. Then it tells of how the original Ebon Knot Cabal used a dread ritual to summon the Prince of 10,000 Leaves to rewrite history so that the natives never released those spirits against them.<br /> It was the last surviving member of that Cabal that started the Red Word, as the meal in a cannibal ritual.<br /> The native shamans were just using a violent spirit as a weapon. That is what Spirit mages do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean the fact that you can't even use the names of the local nations in Boston honestly kind of deflates your argument, the use of cannibal spirits might be a part of the setting but that doesn't mean it can't be overturned. The Ebon Knot cabal can be fully blamed for the entire incident and in fact, if I was writing this expansion to the Boston setting for use I'd make the cannibal spirits an afterthought or even a 10,000 Leaves fantasy which can be scrutinized and torn down by PCs.<br /> <br /> In fact, if I were doing this reimagining I would probably even trouble the idea that the Ebon Knot was confronted primarily with Thyrsus or Spirit-users as a part of a historical fantasy of settler colonialism on the supernatural landscape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25371-elzopilote","name":"elzopilote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25371_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T17:54:19-07:00","id":1325443,"title":"","content":"The idea was based upon what is in the book, a work of fiction. I'm not making an argument, just offering a suggestion based upon what someone else printed as part of the setting.<br /> The honest truth is you can't use real tribes (or other historical groups) accurately without offending someone. No one alive today can accurately say what did or didn't happen as all records are recorded with a biased view point. This is doubly true in an admitted work of fiction.<br /> If I was writing this book the first thing I would do is make up groups and advise that they have no real world counterparts.<br /> I'm sure when the author wrote the book they chose to use cannibal spirits, as opposed to say bear spirits, because they lead to more interesting antagonists.<br /> If you want you can overturn it at your table. You can make anyone the villain, if this book was written at that point in history they probably would have blamed the French, of course you still risk offending someone.<br /> No offense was intended, just a suggestion on how it might be tied into the written setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T09:55:21-07:00","id":1325633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elzopilote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1325400#post1325400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the fact that you can't even use the names of the local nations in Boston honestly kind of deflates your argument,</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you're parroting back the wrong name for the Ebon Noose which isn't terribly impressive either. It reads like you're arguing with 2ptTakrill's somewhat faulty memory of the book, rather than with the book itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T12:18:31-07:00","id":1325697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1325633#post1325633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, you're parroting back the wrong name for the Ebon Noose which isn't terribly impressive either. It reads like you're arguing with 2ptTakrill's somewhat faulty memory of the book, rather than with the book itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact you think the real life nations whose lands were occupied to found Boston are equivalent to a fictional cabal is kind of galling and shows you are completely missing the point here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T12:37:19-07:00","id":1325700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1325697#post1325697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact you think the real life nations whose lands were occupied to found Boston are equivalent to a fictional cabal is kind of galling and shows you are completely missing the point here.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I clearly didn't say that, and your characterisation is highly offensive.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T18:44:18-07:00","id":1326573,"title":"","content":"I like the book as written. Thanks for the ideas guys. I think I like the hidden distillery idea and will likely run with that especially since the spirit familiar of one of the PCs is attracted to alcohol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T15:11:45-08:00","id":1503631,"title":"","content":"Hard to believe, but I'm running Boston 2.0 again tomorrow night with an additional two players.<br /> <br /> The last session was 3.5 years ago for the original players and I've STed the new guys a couple of times to get them used to things and it's gone well.<br /> <br /> I ran the Abedju Cipher with the twist that the cipher's primary purpose is to index the Prince's fragments. The new PCs managed to get the Cipher when the Egyptian exhibit came to Boston. It's led them to investigate the cult of the red word and to look for the original players to help them.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the assault on Wendigo's Sanctum has gone horribly wrong. They traced their way there from leads acquired at Zee's mother's house and managed to defeat the initial wave of Cultists, but when Balam Chang saw his family pendant around Wendigo's neck he lost it and went in for the attack. The Emerald Guard materialized and delivered lethal and aggravated damage. Conora barely manged to co-locate the cabal back to their Sanctum before the situation got worse....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T18:22:02-08:00","id":1503657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1503631#post1503631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hard to believe, but I'm running Boston 2.0 again tomorrow night with an additional two players.<br /> <br /> The last session was 3.5 years ago for the original players and I've STed the new guys a couple of times to get them used to things and it's gone well.<br /> <br /> I ran the Abedju Cipher with the twist that the cipher's primary purpose is to index the Prince's fragments. The new PCs managed to get the Cipher when the Egyptian exhibit came to Boston. It's led them to investigate the cult of the red word and to look for the original players to help them.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the assault on Wendigo's Sanctum has gone horribly wrong. They traced their way there from leads acquired at Zee's mother's house and managed to defeat the initial wave of Cultists, but when Balam Chang saw his family pendant around Wendigo's neck he lost it and went in for the attack. The Emerald Guard materialized and delivered lethal and aggravated damage. Conora barely manged to co-locate the cabal back to their Sanctum before the situation got worse....</div> </div> </div> </div>I might suggest starting a new thread for keeping up with it and getting advice. This one's well lived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T10:38:52-08:00","id":1503687,"title":"","content":"Thanks, but I'd prefer to preserve the history.<br /> <br /> I'm still looking for advice though. I'm guessing the PCs are going to want to investigate Howard's Rock and likely want to destroy it.<br /> <br /> Wendigo, Roi du Sang, Temple Hounds, Emerald Guard, Red Word Cultists and possibly some Chenoo might be enough for the &quot;final fight&quot;, but I'm considering some kind of Acamoth/Gulmoth to be present as well. Something truly horrifying, but still in keeping with the Prince's anti-history. Any ideas?<br /> <br /> Also, do you think Roi du Sang should be an Acanthus?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T13:35:23-08:00","id":1503700,"title":"","content":"What sort of challenge do you want the Acamoth/Gulmoth to pose?<br /> \u2022 A physical threat, possibly to be faced in the final battle?<br /> \u2022 A puzzle that needs to be solved, that otherwise keeps some options closed from the players?<br /> \u2022 A social interaction, that needs to be convinced or manipulated to give way to the PCs?<br /> \u2022 A moral conundrum? It could be an unsolvable one, designed just to make players squirm.<br /> <br /> How did the Intruder get there, and what is its relationship with the Cult?<br /> \u2022 Do you want it to be a discrete entity to be confronted, or more of a force of unnature that needs more creativity to be overcome?<br /> \u2022 Was it purposefully summoned by the Cult, or was it unexpected, possibly a wildcard unaligned with any of the sides?\u200b<br /> \u2022 Is it an inhabitant of the Prince, or a secondary side-effect of reality deteriorating?<br /> <br /> Most importantly: what would your players enjoy in the encounter? What abilities would they like to flex and what aspects of their characters do they want to express?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T07:25:49-08:00","id":1503944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1503700#post1503700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sort of challenge do you want the Acamoth/Gulmoth to pose?<br /> \u2022 A physical threat, possibly to be faced in the final battle?<br /> \u2022 A puzzle that needs to be solved, that otherwise keeps some options closed from the players?<br /> \u2022 A social interaction, that needs to be convinced or manipulated to give way to the PCs?<br /> \u2022 A moral conundrum? It could be an unsolvable one, designed just to make players squirm.<br /> <br /> How did the Intruder get there, and what is its relationship with the Cult?<br /> \u2022 Do you want it to be a discrete entity to be confronted, or more of a force of unnature that needs more creativity to be overcome?<br /> \u2022 Was it purposefully summoned by the Cult, or was it unexpected, possibly a wildcard unaligned with any of the sides?\u200b<br /> \u2022 Is it an inhabitant of the Prince, or a secondary side-effect of reality deteriorating?<br /> <br /> Most importantly: what would your players enjoy in the encounter? What abilities would they like to flex and what aspects of their characters do they want to express?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! These are all really good questions.<br /> <br /> I suppose I'd like a physical threat for the final battle, but with maybe a puzzle that helps fight it or is involved somehow. An interesting idea might be to have something that has turned Balam Chang's brother (now a member of the Red Word) into a physical threat that they need to destroy, but maybe there's a clever solution that can reduce the threat so that they can possibly de-escalate and save him instead of killing him.<br /> <br /> Another thing. The rules have changed between 1e and 2e and I'm wondering if the Temple of Holy Devouring would be an Abyssal Verge in 2e or still in Shadow accessible by a Shadow Iris?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 03-01-2023, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T03:15:09-08:00","id":1504922,"title":"","content":"I'm so sorry! I missed your response. I'm at work, so I can only repost another &quot;boss battle&quot; you could use:<br /> <br /> (The Link won't show up. Look on the last page of &quot;[2ED] Boston &amp; New England setting&quot;)<br /> <br /> You could repurpose this and have the Cultists transform the brother into a living Iris into the Prince. There would have to be some way to heal him, and a specific trigger that would make him go haywire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 03-09-2023, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T12:01:30-08:00","id":1504962,"title":"","content":"No worries. Good idea. I'll check out the other thread.<br /> <br /> I'll give everyone a chronicle update though:<br /> <br /> Chapter 17<br /> <br /> After recuperating for a day, Balam (Perfected Adept, Arrow), Baron (Moros, Detective, FC), Nyder (Acanthus, Historian, Mysterium) and Silas (Mastigos, Psychologist, FC) got together, on advice from Potestas &amp; Ferrum, to compare notes on the Red Word, while NPC Agdos went to research more about the cult in New York. They figured out that the Abedju Cipher could index the Prince's Fragments and that the Fragments were Abyssal in nature. They also ransacked Zee's apartment one last time and found Ezekiel Johnston's business card. He's the chef/owner of the Howard's Rock Hotel.<br /> <br /> They decided to travel to Howard's Rock and investigate the hotel. They got a room at the hotel and ate dinner there. Nyder has Spirit so they finally noticed the Spirit Ravens following them and figured out that they were mostly following Balam (his brother is secretly in the Red Word). They &quot;retired&quot; for the evening and decided to lay a trap for anyone who might mess with them during the night. They co-located back to Silas' apartment after Nyder Divined the next time the door to their hotel room would be opened - just after midnight.<br /> <br /> Chapter 18<br /> <br /> Silas web-weaved his way to Strong sympathy to the hotel room and opened a portal from his kitchen to the hotel room bathroom door way. He also opened a Scrying window in the hotel room. He was burning through mana and had taken about 4 resistant bashing from containing multiple Paradoxes. Baron decided to turn Twilight with Ghost Gate and use the portal to lie in wait in the hotel room.<br /> <br /> Wendigo used Web of Life at the doorway which detected Baron (I was iffy on this one, but decided he was still &quot;Life&quot; even in Twilight). This pinged Baron's PMS so he wisely cast Suppress Life on himself and disappeared (won the Clash of Wills) from Wendigo's &quot;radar&quot;. Wendigo (activating AMS) found it strange and flanked by an Emerald Guard he Annie, Cameron and 3 other cultists with shotguns entered the room to investigate.<br /> <br /> Baron was bold and cast Ghost Gate on the Jade Pendant (Balam's family heirloom and the Eye of Ammut, a Scelesti Soul Stone) and Wendigo failed to counter it with Prime 2. Baron grabbed the Pendant and dashed through the Portal. The Portal was Keyed and even though it was discovered, the Emerald Guard and cultists couldn't use it. \u200bNyder cast the Weight of Years on the floor and Baron followed with Decay and the floor collapsed after taking 9 structural damage. Wendigo avoided falling and Emerald Guard could levitate, but the cultists all plummeted down a floor taking about half their health in Bashing damage. Wendigo ordered a retreat just as Silas collapsed his Portal and Scrying window.<br /> <br /> I didn't expect Baron to get the Pendant. He handed it to Balam who used focused Prime mage sight to peal back it's Opacity 4 mystery and reveal it's nature as a Hunger inducing, Scelesti Legacy carrying Soul Stone centuries old with Cannibalistic and Abyssal Resonance.<br /> <br /> We ended with Agdos calling Balam to tell them that she managed to find Agartha's (devoured by the Shinje) Sleepwalker research assistant in New York and learn a lot more about the Red Word and asked to meet them to discuss everything ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 03-09-2023, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T15:21:23-07:00","id":1507611,"title":"","content":"Here is an update:<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 19</b><br /> <br /> Primarily an investigation and roleplaying session. They meet with Agdos to compare notes and learn more about the Fragments and the Cult of the Red Word. They decide to raid Wendigo's sanctum again to learn more about what the Red Word are up to in Howard's Rock.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 20</b><br /> <br /> A big battle at Wendigo's sanctum against two Emerald Guard, a Temple Hound and Cameron (armed with a Fire Spirit Fetish). They are victorious thanks to Balam (Perfected Adept) just pummeling everything in sight. Silas (Mastigos) begins questioning Cameron who stabs a knife into his eye rather than be questioned. Silas still manages to learn (Read the Depths) that Wendigo is in the Temple of Holy Devouring preparing the Summer Solstice &quot;feast&quot; with the two other members of the Rightful Kings cabal [I allowed three questions given Cameron's quick suicide]. Baron (Moros) callously Soul Jar's Cameron's departing soul and executes the subdued Temple Hound. He loses a 2nd dot of Wisdom and gains an Obsessed with Thwarting the Red Word condition. Nyder (Acanthus w/Spirit) ends up with the Fire Staff. He's also holding the Abedju Cipher which can index Fragments. Baron investigates the area and finds a letter from Roi du Sang about the Cult's plans to usher Rhukavira into the world at Howard's Rock on the Summer Solstice. On the way back to Boston they learn that Wally the Green Monster hasn't shown up to a Red Sox game in 3 days.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 21</b><br /> <br /> Just a two player session: Baron and Silas travel to Waltman's Neck to retrieve the Ghost of Ryan O'Connor (a summer student murdered by Annie Crowther in her mother's kitchen). They get him back to The Loft (Sanctum) and Baron ritually casts Quicken Ghost to turn him into a Rank 3 super ghost. He negotiates with him and Ryan agrees to help the Cabal to get his revenge on the Cult.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 22</b><br /> <br /> The cabal spends a day on ritual magic to bolster their offensive and defensive capabilities. Balam recruits Ikazuchi to help him persuade Ferrum to assemble the Exalted Knights of the Gryphon to assault Howard's Rock before they manage to summon an Abyssal incursion. Agdos calls to say she will return tomorrow and will help. Maggie Yang calls Baron to ask him again if he has found the woman they rescued from ritual sacrifice in the basement of the Coptic church (Chapter 10 or so). He's put her off a couple times, but this time he doesn't know what she's talking about. He doesn't remember the woman (Debra Henley). Perfect Recall doesn't reveal anything either. Nyder postulates that she's been erased from the timeline. [I decided a long time ago in an earlier chronicle that when someone is devoured at the Temple people forget them according to Sympathy, Maggie has Medium sympathy and Baron has weak Sympathy, so she is &quot;erased &quot; to him first].<br /> <br /> Roi du Sang (Rightful Kings, Acanthus w/Space) casts Divination on Nyder to find out when he will next be alone. He corners him in an Ikea (getting furniture for his room at The Loft) and demands the Abedju Cipher or &quot;else&quot;. Nyder (wisely) figures he can't win and gives him the Cipher [The Cult needs this to verify that the sequence of 132 Fragments they've compiled to bring Rhukavira into existence are in the correct order before they start the ritual on the Summer Solstice]. Roi du Sang retrieves Wendigo's Fire Staff from The Loft as well.<br /> <br /> They find out that the President of Harvard and a Congress woman are also missing. Nyder investigates the congressional office (steals her fountain pen for Sympathy) and meets Ogma (of Gloria Mundi fame, that I always turn into a Guardian police investigator for the Consilium). He tells Nyder that Cardinal White (prominent Catholic), the last winner of the Boston Marathon, and Gilbert Lancaster (wealthy philanthropist socialite, also from Gloria Mundi) are all missing as well. What's going on? [The Red Word are going to sacrifice prominent influencers in Boston as part of the ritual to bring Rhukavira into existence through the gap in history provided by their wailing devoured souls. To make this even more personal to Baron (Moros, PI) I've decided that Maggie Yang (prominent Journalist/blogger) will also be abducted as the final flourish.]<br /> <br /> Ferrum agrees to assemble the Knights (4 Arrows) and Balam is to outline his battle plan for attacking Howard's Rock at a meeting on 6/19 (two days before the ritual) at 3 PM at the Academy. Agdos and Ogma will also be there. Silas and Balam sneak into Fenway to get Wally the Green Monster's spare baseball cap so they have some Sympathy to him.<br /> <br /> The session ended with everyone forming a crazy idea to use Temporal Summons to visit Baron in the past when he still remembered Debra Henley so that he could remember her enough to gain some Sympathy to her. [This should fail as she's already been devoured at the Temple and doesn't even exist anymore in the timeline. Baron <i>never </i>knew her. If he talks to Maggie again before she is kidnapped, she won't remember her either anymore and at some point I'll just tell them &quot;Debra who?&quot; and that they can't investigate someone who doesn't exist anymore. Even their notes on her don't exist anymore.]<br /> <br /> In my next post I'll outline my plans and ask anyone who wants to help me shape the final couple chapters of this story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 04-06-2023, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T14:47:36-07:00","id":1507960,"title":"","content":"Please help! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> At the end of the last session I forgot to mention that Baron (Moros, PI) asked Davey Jones to cast a Fate spell on him so that he would &quot;encounter Debra Henley again&quot;. This could have amazing story potential or turn into nothing. I'm looking for advice on this one. Debra was already consumed in the Temple of Holy Devouring and has been erased from history. Path one is that Baron is now Fated to be devoured in the temple. Path two is that the spell does nothing as Debra is someone no longer a part of reality. Not sure which way to go on this one.<br /> <br /> As it stands right now, The Nemean (still 2010) is having the regular Summer Solstice gathering of Mages at The Cormant House in Salem. Most area Mages are going, with the exception of those assaulting Howard's Rock to stop The Red Word from summoning Rhukavira (which they don't yet understand would replace all of Boston).<br /> <br /> The Mages who have signed up for the assault:<br /> <br /> - All four of the Exalted Knights of the Gryphon (the muscle)<br /> - Agdos from the Brotherhood of Ineffable Truth (looking for lore/answers)<br /> - Davey Jones and Rabid Annie from the Dead Wrens (maybe just for transport by ship)<br /> - The PCs (Moros w/Rank 3 Ghost ally, Perfected Adept, Mastigos/Cryptologos, Acanthus w/Spirit)<br /> <br /> It's 11 Mages against:<br /> <br /> - The Rightful Kings cabal of 3 Gnosis 4 Mages - Wendigo (Spirit/Life 4), Roi du Sang (Time 4, Fate/Space 3), Feach (Space 4, Forces/Mind 3)<br /> - Emerald Guard (Rank 2 Abyssal Cannibal Spirits, as many as needed)<br /> - Temple Hounds (as many as needed)<br /> - Enhanced Red Word Cultists (as many as needed)<br /> - Balefire Spirits (as many as needed)<br /> - ??? (I'll talk about this later)<br /> <br /> The plan will be up to the Perfected Adept PC (as a further mentoring exercise) and I've decided that Ogma, though not going on the assault will use a Shield of Chronos to mess up Roi du Sang's attempt at Divining when the assault will be. There will be a suggestion to get help from a Spirit ally (likely Wa'Bun, Spirit of the East Wind, I've used in other Chronicles).<br /> <br /> I'm ok with a few NPC mages getting killed or even a PC if they really mess up.<br /> <br /> <b>Here are my questions</b>:<br /> <br /> 1. How should I split up the assault? I'd generally like for the PCs to be doing the important stuff, but Ferrum would at least want to lead the charge in some way.<br /> 2. How can the Temple of Holy Devouring be destroyed? For that matter how does anything from the Prince's anti-history get shunted back into the Abyss? I was thinking of having some of Rhukavira get summoned before they are able to interrupt the ritual. How would Sleepers react to this? It's not Supernal, but that's a huge supernatural phenomenon for Sleepers to witness.<br /> 3. It would be fantastic if one of the last things they need to do is confront Balam's brother that joined the cult. I was thinking of him having volunteered to became some kind of powerful Horror in keeping with the Prince. I'm having hard time thinking of what this could be. I'm not trying to game the outcome, but ideally they subdue him/it and Baron, who has executed two Temple Hounds already, decides to execute Balam's brother. It's something the PC would do and would be awesome roleplaying material. I'd like to give him the opportunity to lose more Wisdom and create party drama. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I know I wrote a lot and we're playing in two days, but any help would be greatly appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T03:55:33-07:00","id":1508014,"title":"","content":"About Debra Henley and the Fate spell. It's best to choose if you want to serve your players with a shocking plot twist or escalating tension. If you choose tension, assume that the new Fate is already tainted by the Abyss and out of Davy Jones' control. He would likely warn the PC's about this, which plays into your hands. A malfunctioning spell may have all kinds of dangerous effects, up to summoning Debra's Abyssal Imprint (from the<i> Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss</i> sourcebook).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you can discard the idea of the Spell being tainted. Make it known that Fate is helping characters along towards the Temple, until they learn that Baron is about to meet his doom. It could be rather rude to erase your player's PC like that so be sure to either give him a good chance of saving himself, or prepare a campaign set within the Prince of 100.000 Leaves. The erased characters may very well still be there.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, do tell them the Spell went wrong, but that it also helps them along towards the Temple. They will face a dilemma that way.<br /> <br /> As for other questions:<br /> 1. Tactics are not my comfort zone. Still, perhaps you could run a session based on drafting a plan and have Ferrum lead that meeting. That way the players aren't forced to think of everything, but can still offer their ideas for you to use. Even if they decide that all the important stuff is better left to other Mages, pivotal events may fall upon them through happenstance. Factors that can pull PCs into action are: Baron's Fate spell, Balam's connection to his brother, Individuals within the Cult following their own agendas (cannibal twins out for revenge, Sanctifier of the Meek's attempts at conversion, Wendigo wanting to reclaim the Pendant).<br /> <br /> 2. The obvious solution is destroying all the Leaves and erasing them from living memory, or at the very least making sure they don't occupy the same place (or mind). The challenges with that are many, first of them being that the Temple will be around for far longer. If the outcome of the story is that the Consillium is rebuilt around keeping the Temple quarantined, then that is an interesting outcome. The <i>more</i> obvious solution is explosives. Lots of them. Even if you can't shunt an Intrusion back into the Abyss, you may just try to destroy it.<br /> If you let Rhukavira manifest, you may go several routes. The first is that Sleepers do see and react to it with either willful ignorance or conspirational fervor. Strange things do happen in the world of CofD, and this will be a prominent one. The second is that more of Rhukavira manifests, but either in an out of the way location, or Sleepers are convinced it was always there. This is whole-sale reality editing, not mere translocation. The Veil will be maintained, but the Prince still gains a greater foothold near Boston.<br /> <br /> 3. Ask your players (especially Balam's) how they feel about that plot thread, and what they think would be most poetically appropriate. Give them that, but not in the way they expect. That's the best I can offer.\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T10:50:14-07:00","id":1508052,"title":"","content":"Thanks so much for your help.<br /> <br /> I love your idea of the Fate spell causing an Abyssal Imprint of Debra to manifest. That could be cool. I own the book and will read up on it. It's a good way of having there be unintended shenanigans without me damning a PC to end up in the the Abyss. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I also really like the idea that the Temple become quarantined by the Consilium. May be a chance to bring Shadow Chorus into the game as Guardians. I'd really like to bring a pyramid with lectern of bone (like the picture in the book) with the Sanctifier of the Meek into existence as the ritual gets started in the hopes that players would interogate the Acamoth and learn the true nature of the Prince just before they go to Howard's Rock. It would allow some exposition so they could get the whole &quot;cool&quot; factor of the Prince, but I'd be open to other ways of unraveling the whole Mystery completely if you have any suggestions.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on a final Horror from the Abyss confrontation? At this point in time I'm thinking of having Balam's brother be a Temple Hound claimed by something from the Prince's reality. What's the typical way of &quot;curing&quot; someone claimed by a Spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 04-11-2023, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T13:50:51-07:00","id":1508071,"title":"","content":"Happy to help.<br /> <br /> Claim is a Manifestation Condition, and those can be outright ended with <i>Banishment</i> (Spirit 4). The possessing Spirit may also choose to disentangle from the host, but I don't remember how long that process takes. Lesser Spells may help in facilitating that, but again, I don't know how they interact with Claimed specifically - casting <i>Command Spirit</i> (Spirit 2) with an order to &quot;Leave this man!&quot; might work, or it might not. Ultimately, even if the exorcism succeeds, the brother is still a Temple Hound, and likely suffering aftereffects from his flesh being reconfigured back and forth.<br /> <br /> You've asked for advice about this confrontation before, and I'm pretty proud of the response I shared back then. The only thing I'm able to add is &quot;What kind of entity would want to possess a Temple Hound?&quot;. A Spirit Noble of Temple Hounds seeking to broaden the hunt? A Missionary who botched its arrival and got trapped? A refugee (or multiple refugees) from the Prince desperate to leave that realm and latching on to whoever it can? A Gatekeeper (Zuul!) that stabilizes the connection between the Prince and reality? Something from the unformed Abyss that stumbled in, corrosive to both reality and the Prince?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T13:57:27-07:00","id":1508073,"title":"","content":"Sorry I'm being such a pain. I like the response from way back and used it in my other game, but was looking for something a little different this time. The Gatekeeper idea seems cool as it would be something deliberate that Feach (Mastigos) might be trying to set up. Is there a reason why the Gateway would require a living host like Balam's brother?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T14:30:55-07:00","id":1508076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1508073#post1508073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a reason why the Gateway would require a living host like Balam's brother?</div> </div> </div> </div>First idea that comes to mind: The Prince embodies human cannibalism - a violation done by a person, one flesh subsuming another. Even a mighty Spirit is not a full person and doesn't even have flesh. It needs to Claim a human to contain all the necessary symbolism to refine Resonance with the Prince.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, Abyss is empowered by Wisdom and Integrity loss. To enhance the connection, the Intruder needs a soul and mind to grind town into delirium and incoherence. Since the brother is an important NPC, it could be neat to figure out if the process makes use of his personality, or discards it like trash. The former might tie the encounter to his and Baron's relationship. The latter explicitly makes it all unfair - Abyss not caring who suffers for it.<br /> <br /> In fact you could determine is there was a reason that the brother found the Soul Stone, or if it's all just an awful coincidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T16:30:03-07:00","id":1508083,"title":"","content":"Awesome stuff. Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T01:05:36-07:00","id":1508125,"title":"","content":"One more silly thing. This might be too late for your campaign, but here's a 2:32 minute review of Boston by Overly Sarcastic Productions:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iTbpxDHOff0\" target=\"_blank\">LINK</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T14:35:07-07:00","id":1508392,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 23</b><br /> <br /> Another RP/planning session.<br /> <br /> They decided to attack the day of the Solstice to disrupt the Red Word ritual at Howard's Rock (132 Fragments of the Prince that would bring Rhukavira into the Fallen World). Then Roi du Sang penetrated Silas' Ward and survived two Counterspell attempts to cast Divination on the cabal to determine when the attack would come (unbeknownst to them).<br /> <br /> They met with the Exalted Knights of the Gryphon, Agdos, and Ogma who cast Shield of Chronos on the meeting and then suggested they move the time table up by a day. [I decided that this would mess up the Divination and left it as a cautionary tale. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ] Davey Jones and Rabid Annie crashed the meeting and agreed to help and suggested an assault by ship using the Hawk of Guangdong (from Beast of Burden).<br /> <br /> In the end they decided the PCs w/Rabid Annie &amp; the Ghost of Ryan O'Connor would infiltrate the Temple by land and that the Gryphons, Agdos and Davey Jones would assault the Temple of Holy Devouring by sea and create enough of a distraction to help the PCs get into the Temple. [I liked this as I could have a narrative NPC group and only worry about the mechanics of the PC group].<br /> <br /> <b>Questions:</b><br /> <br /> 1. Should the Temple be assailable by cannon-fire from the Hawk of Guangdong even though it's in an Abyssal Verge? I'm thinking yes because it was brought into the Fallen World with 13 Fragments of the Prince, but I'm still uncertain. The way it was written there's only an Iris at the base of the Temple to gain access, but Abyssal Verges weren't as much of a thing when Boston Unveiled was written.<br /> <br /> 2. If the Temple is in Twilight would a Space(?) mage need to open Irises to enable the canon-fire to target the Temple? This could be an interesting complication as Ogma decided he wasn't up for a fight and bowed out, but he has Space 4 and could teleport in if needed to open the &quot;hole&quot; needed to assault the Temple. What do you think?<br /> <br /> That's it for now.<br /> <br /> The PCs are trying to rescue the sacrificial victims and kill all of the Rightful Kings (Wendigo, Roi du Sang, and Feach), as well as secure the Fragments for &quot;safe keeping&quot; by the Mysterium. I'm trying to design 4 or 5 encounters for the PC as they make their way into the final ritual chamber and watch in horror as Balam's brother is being turned into a Gateway into the Prince's reality. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks again for all your help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T05:30:58-07:00","id":1508430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1508392#post1508392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Should the Temple be assailable by cannon-fire from the Hawk of Guangdong even though it's in an Abyssal Verge? I'm thinking yes because it was brought into the Fallen World with 13 Fragments of the Prince, but I'm still uncertain. The way it was written there's only an Iris at the base of the Temple to gain access, but Abyssal Verges weren't as much of a thing when Boston Unveiled was written.<br /> <br /> 2. If the Temple is in Twilight would a Space(?) mage need to open Irises to enable the canon-fire to target the Temple? This could be an interesting complication as Ogma decided he wasn't up for a fight and bowed out, but he has Space 4 and could teleport in if needed to open the &quot;hole&quot; needed to assault the Temple. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I read it (and it is ambiguous), the Temple &quot;landed&quot; in the Shadow. The aforementioned Iris is located near the shore and leads from the Material into the Shadow, which is how Cultists gain access. A cannon assault would require the NPCs to move their ship into the Shadow, which is difficult, but possible.<br /> <br /> I you already planned the Temple to be in Twilight, you need to decide which frequency it's in. Death, Spirit, Mind or other. The relevant Arcanum can open Irises to that frequency, and cannonballs can be blasted through. Alternatively, the NPCs can cast Correspondence (Space 1) to learn the Key to the Cultists' Verge, open it from afar and aim really well (Compelling of Space should be enough to deal with the dice penalties).<br /> <br /> If you need to design encounters, at least some of them may take place in the Shadow that has been twisted by the Temple's presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 04-15-2023, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T07:13:18-07:00","id":1508441,"title":"","content":"Do you think the Temple would have manifested in the Shadow or do you think that's just a hold-over from 1e because Abyssal Verges weren't really a thing? In my thinking the Prince is an Annunaki that is replacing reality as Fragments are properly joined. Why would it manifest in Shadow instead of just plain being there in the Fallen World?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T08:35:30-07:00","id":1508449,"title":"","content":"When <i>Boston Unveiled</i> was published Abyssal Verges weren't a thing. I assume if it was written today, the Temple would be made into a Verge. However, whenever the Abyss is involved, consistent metaphysics can be discarded, especially if it's in favor of players having fun. You could also assume that the Temple doesn't &quot;come&quot; from the Abyss - it's merely the Shadow beginning to reflect the Prince instead of the Fallen World. The Cultists would be trying to pull the Prince even closer, so that the Material becomes overwritten as well.<br /> <br /> I believe the following has priority: Your PCs and NPCs already made a plan based on information they learned. You don't want to retroactively lie to them. Did you lead your players to believe that the Temple is in the Material (or Twilight)? Hold on to that, and reshape the metaphysics to fit. Did they wrongly assume that the Temple will be easy to reach? In that case you can surprise them, make the plan with the ship pointless, and force your NPCs to improvise a new plan during the assault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T17:52:04-07:00","id":1508592,"title":"","content":"Wise advice. Thanks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T09:05:41-07:00","id":1509284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help#post1095319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought I'd create a thread similar to the ask a simple question thread, but more focused on setting and chronicle help, so please feel free to ask your own questions regarding getting help for your chronicles.<br /> <br /> I started my 2nd 2e Chronicle today, also based in Boston (because I know it, having run 60 sessions in Boston over the years).<br /> <br /> I have two players that have chosen workable concepts: Obrimos Perfected Adept &amp; Moros Necromancer Investigator.<br /> <br /> My third player has a really strange character concept: Acanthus junk-art scrapper with Matter as his 3rd Arcana and a rank 2 Raven familiar that is a Spirit of Greed. He's in the Adamantine Arrow and wanted his own Sanctum &amp; Hallow (2 dots) which is a Sacred Tree in the secluded area of a city park.<br /> <br /> I know it's off the wall, but this player really wants all this eclectic stuff and I really believe in letting people play the characters they want to play.<br /> <br /> He's never played a WoD game before and I'd really like to figure out how to make this character work. Here are my questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Can a Raven Greed spirit make any sense?<br /> <br /> 2. Can a Sanctum based around a Sacred Tree in the middle of Boston Commons park make any sense? How can this be a Safe Place, for instance?<br /> <br /> 3. Is there an Acanthus Legacy with Matter as a 3rd Arcana make any sense?<br /> <br /> I'd really appreciate assistance making this jumble of stuff all fit together somehow, because let's face it: The idea of an Acanthus Arrow Junk-artist Matter mage tasked with protecting a Sacred Tree with his Raven Spirit could be very cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>With Fate, you can use shielding/ruling to Prevent people from ever being fated to enter or something similar. This could make a sufficiently secluded area secure even without traditional security measures. People would just never find it or choose to go there under normal circumstances. Creating a Safe Place with dots equal to potency seems like a decent effect for such a spell. Representing it with just pure Merit dots would just be a way to not bother with the bookkeeping of replacing the spell with a higher version when you spend XP to increase it or to deal with the particulars of spending WP dots and regaining them. There are likely to be consequences to &quot;walling off&quot; what once might have been freely accessible to other supernatural entities though.<br /> <br /> I dont personally know of such a Legacy, but canonically Mages create personal legacies all the time. Joining an old storied Legacy is cool, but realistically I think most Mages are rocking personalized Legacies. I also think most of them dont get past One or two attainments. Anyway, you can probably do something with the idea of &quot;One man's trash...etc&quot;. At least, thats what comes to mind for me. Off hand though, everyone starts with at least 3 different arcana at chargen by default(just the way the rules work out). You don't really need a Legacy right away just because they started with some Matter dots. Only Arcana they aren't allowed to start with is Forces as an Acanthus.<br /> <br /> Raven greed spirit makes total sense to me and others already said good things about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24407-radriel7","name":"Radriel7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24407_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T17:00:52-07:00","id":1509537,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your insights","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T10:18:36-07:00","id":1511381,"title":"","content":"Thanks eveyone for all the help. Things are going well in the Chronicle and I can post an update if anyone wants. I only have one question from last session:<br /> <br /> Is Ban really completely impenetrable unless you use Space or Prime to penetrate or dispel it? I don't have a problem with it, but wanted to make sure I was doing it right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T10:40:16-07:00","id":1511385,"title":"","content":"Hey, I'm already invested. I'm happy to see any updates you're willing to share.<br /> <br /> As for the Ban spell, here's a quote from the book:<br /> <i>&quot;Magic that manipulates space, like a teleportation power or <u>the ability to step from one world to another</u>, provokes a Clash of Wills to allow ingress or egress.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> If the character has supernatural power to move through the Gauntlet, or into some half-formed Abyssal otherworld, that might be enough to escape (with Clash of Wills). Powers that let you escape bindings and entrapment should count as well.<br /> <br /> If your Ban is combined with a different Arcanum to only affect some phenomena, like adding Life to only trap human beings, the subject might transform themselves into something else to escape. Perhaps using Veiling could be enough (with Clash of Wills).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T11:50:58-07:00","id":1512608,"title":"","content":"Here is the latest update:<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 24</b>:<br /> <br /> We began with Nyder (Acanthus) delving deep into the history of the Jade Pendant with Postcog. He saw it's creation as a Soul Stone and it's travels through time from Egypt to South Korea. He saw many wearers of the pendant murdered over centuries of travel. The last two murderers were identified by voice through Telepathy/Perfect Recall to be Balam's Father (20 years ago) and Balam's Brother (3 months ago). Balam was dismayed by this and called his Father to demand answers but he didn't pick up (Korean time zone difference). The pendant was further scrutinized (by Baron) and found to be cursed to induce The Hunger over time (as outlined earlier in this thread). I considered the Mystery of The Eye of Ammut the Devourer to be solved. Balam immediately removed it from his person and put it in a safe at The Loft.<br /> <br /> At this point it was time to meet the others at Pier 86 in Boston Harbor. When they arrived they were surprised to see Ogma, but he decided to provide remote tactical support in the form of Scrying and Telepathy between the two teams assaulting Howard's Rock and wanted hair from Balam and Ferrum to make it work. Davy Jones had everyone Swear an Oath to stay true to the mission of &quot;eliminating the so-called Rightful Kings, rescuing their sacrificial victims and stopping the accursed Abyssal ritual to bring Rukhavira into this Fallen World or may I be struck Blind until dawn.&quot; Everyone received Steadfast, Inspired and +3 on a skill for 3 uses.<br /> <br /> They set out on the Hawk of Guangdong (acquired by the PCs and gifted to the Dead Wrens in Beast of Burden). A few miles from Howard's Rock, the PCs with Rabid Annie &amp; the Ghost of Ryan O'Connor used a life boat to make their way to the docks at Howard's Rock, Invisible, Surpernally Veiled, Without a Trace, with Suppressed Auras. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> They managed to narrowly avoid detection by some Red Word fishermen on the docks, but made their way up the Temple of Holy Devouring steps. Along the way they observed the lecturn of bone (as depicted in Boston Unveiled) on a side plateau where some cultists were worshipping under the direction of The Sanctifier of the Meek (see earlier in thread). Silas noticed that it was an Acamoth, but they decided to ignore it and press on.<br /> <br /> Ferrum's sea team began assaulting the Temple with explosive shells (old cannons transformed by Agdos with Matter 4) taking chunks out of some upper areas, which caused Feach (the 3rd Rightful King Mage) to initiate 3 Bans - one by one every 2 turns to protect the Temple towers. Under Acceleration from Nyder the group managed to get inside the middle tower just before the last Ban closed them inside.<br /> <br /> They were immediately ambushed by 2 Emerald Guard, 3 Temple Hounds and 9 Enhanced Red Word Cultists. They were Invisible (which in our game inflicts the half-blind tilt: -3 to hit and 1/2 defense, as we say that people give away their position a little when attacking etc...). Balam rushed to attack but a DF had him Prone at the feet of both Emerald Guard and a couple Temple Hounds. The fight was engaged with Rabid Annie cutting into Temple Hounds with her flaming cutlass, Baron training his pistol on the enemy and Nyder using Chronos Curse (a Praxis) to slow many of them down.<br /> <br /> The session ended dramatically when Silas Reached heavily (+1 Paradox inside the Temple) and poured everything he could into using Psychic Domination to instruct all 9 gun wielding cultists to commit suicide. They did!<br /> <br /> more to follow ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 05-24-2023, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T16:11:31-07:00","id":1515701,"title":"","content":"Any rules for Abyssally tainted Ghosts anywhere in either 1e or or 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T16:30:15-07:00","id":1515703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1515701#post1515701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any rules for Abyssally tainted Ghosts anywhere in either 1e or or 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t recall any, nor an example to build on, in 2e. I think<br /> <b>Night Horrors: The Unbidden</b><br /> had an example or two, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T03:25:09-07:00","id":1515734,"title":"","content":"<i>Grimoire of Grimoires</i> had the Ialdabaoth Codex. A book that acted as a prison for Abyssal entities, some of which were tainted Ghosts. I don't remember if they had actual <i>rules</i>, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T12:46:35-07:00","id":1515771,"title":"","content":"What I'm wondering is if the Death 3 Mage in our game should just be able to control an Abyssally tainted Ghost or not, or if there should be some complications....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T14:46:27-07:00","id":1515789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1515771#post1515771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm wondering is if the Death 3 Mage in our game should just be able to control an Abyssally tainted Ghost or not, or if there should be some complications....</div> </div> </div> </div>It does work, but with some difficulty, I guess.<br /> <br /> Maybe the ghost counts as a Sleeper for calculating Paradox. Maybe any spell affecting it flat-out costs +1 Reach. Maybe Perfecting and Fraying spells cast on it are inverted. Maybe it persuades you to take it as a Familiar, secretly offering to teach you Befouled Rotes in return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T14:51:07-07:00","id":1515790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1515771#post1515771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm wondering is if the Death 3 Mage in our game should just be able to control an Abyssally tainted Ghost or not, or if there should be some complications....</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that attempting to control an Abyss-tainted <i>anything</i> is likely to have complications - at its most mechanically simple, I could see increasing Paradox dice by its Rank when interacting with it via Death Arcanum since you're tangling with something channelling / touched by the Abyss. Could be that its Anchors are similarly channelling Abyssal energies into the Fallen World, or that it can create an Abyssal environmental tilt with a numen, there's a lot of ways you can take it to make interacting with it more dangerous or risky. Gulmoth and Acamoth are mentioned as having 'unique and bizarre Influences, Numina and other, weirder expressions of their corrosive natures'.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T05:45:55-07:00","id":1515852,"title":"","content":"There was a thread of homebrew aspects and Numina for Abyssal entities:<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/925972-2e-abyssal-aspects-and-numina\">LINK</a><br /> Maybe some of them could be of use. The important thing to remember is that Abyssal corruption could manifest as <i>anything</i>, even when anchored to a Ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T20:22:43-07:00","id":1515923,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone. The Moros ended up going a different way with it. I'll explain later. \ud83d\ude01","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T16:32:20-07:00","id":1521156,"title":"","content":"Can anyone think of a cool name for a Spirit historian Legacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T16:41:53-07:00","id":1521157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1521156#post1521156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone think of a cool name for a Spirit historian Legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Manifest Zeitgeist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T15:21:36-07:00","id":1521622,"title":"","content":"I like it quite a bit.<br /> <br /> I could use some help with it if anyone has time.<br /> <br /> My issue is that this is an Acanthus that wants Spirit as a Ruling Arcana. He already has Know Spirit as a Rote and Postcognition as a Praxis.<br /> <br /> In an ideal world the Legacy attainments wouldn't overlap with those, but would be Spirit attainments with optional Time and maybe Fate.<br /> <br /> It's hard to imagine the Legacy without having Know Spirit as the 1st attainment and Postcognition as the Optional Time 2nd attainment, but I'm open to other ideas.<br /> <br /> The character wants to be a Spirit Historian essentially.<br /> <br /> My current breakdown for the 1st couple attainments is Know Spirit/Momentary Flux and then Shadow Walk/Postcognition, but I don't completely love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T15:45:34-07:00","id":1521625,"title":"","content":"If you want them to avoid losing Know Spirit to Attainment overlap, make it an Exorcist\u2019s Eye Attainment instead, possibly with Death being the optional for at least the Initiate. Simplest would be to just make it Lasting / always-on. If you need a drawback to counteract that extra point of Reach, then have any Spirits observed with it be automatically aware that the Mage can see them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-29-2023, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T18:41:05-07:00","id":1521637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1521622#post1521622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it quite a bit.<br /> <br /> I could use some help with it if anyone has time.<br /> <br /> My issue is that this is an Acanthus that wants Spirit as a Ruling Arcana. He already has Know Spirit as a Rote and Postcognition as a Praxis.<br /> <br /> In an ideal world the Legacy attainments wouldn't overlap with those, but would be Spirit attainments with optional Time and maybe Fate.<br /> <br /> It's hard to imagine the Legacy without having Know Spirit as the 1st attainment and Postcognition as the Optional Time 2nd attainment, but I'm open to other ideas.<br /> <br /> The character wants to be a Spirit Historian essentially.<br /> <br /> My current breakdown for the 1st couple attainments is Know Spirit/Momentary Flux and then Shadow Walk/Postcognition, but I don't completely love it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see. <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> notes that Acanthus view Spirit as the forbidden places in the stories and the darkness beyond the light. So, Acanthus who view history as strange times in a strange land would lean to Spirit as means of interacting with the spirits that actually lived through history, and familiarizing herself with that unfamiliar world.<br /> <br /> With a theme like above, something like......<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>First</b><br /> <br /> The historian inquires a spirit's history as Know Spirit (Spirit \u2022), but with the list of available facts expanded to include the following:<br /> <br /> <i>\u2022 How long, roughly, has the spirit been here, and has it ever Manifested or fell into slumber in the meantime?<br /> <br /> \u2022 What actions, broadly, has the spirit taken here?</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u2022 How has the spirit, if ever, changed in Rank or Influences?</i><br /> <br /> Notably, the first time a historian inquires a spirit via this Attainment, she always gets an answer to one of the above expanded questions (chosen by the player) in addition to whatever this Attainment's Potency allows for, circumventing Withstand.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 1<br /> <br /> When inquiring the above expanded questions, the historian may now pin-point when it happened. This cannot circumvent lacunae; if one has happened between the historian's inquiry and the relevant event's true moment of happening, the Attainment provides the lacuna as the answer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Second</b><br /> <br /> The historian awakens the spirits to relive the past. This functions as Coaxing the Spirits (Spirit \u2022), but instead of acting in accordance with its nature, the spirit or its representation reenacts a past action to its best ability. Reach is assigned to instant casting and sensory range.<br /> <br /> The reenactment is performed on the spot; if a spirit clawed at a human, for example, it will make clawing gestures in thin air instead of flying off to maim the original victim again.<br /> <br /> The historian must specify the exact past action he wants to see reenacted. Alternatively, he may designate a past moment, and have the subject reenact what it did in that moment.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 2<br /> <br /> After coaxing the subject, the historian may trigger a vision as per Postcognition (Time \u2022), with Reach assigned to instant casting and retaining awareness (Defense) in the present. Temporal Sympathy can be applied as usual.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Third</b><br /> <br /> Resonance is the means by which the world connects Once and Now, and the historian works to encourage it. She may spend 1 Mana to 'summon' past Resonances of an area, with a ritual that takes time as her Gnosis-derived ritual interval. (Quick reference: three hours at Gnosis 1, one hour at Gnosis 3, thirty minutes at Gnosis 5, ten minutes at Gnosis 7, and one minute at Gnosis 9)<br /> <br /> The summoning lasts for hours equal to the historian's Spirit dots, during which mundane attempts to weaken the summoned Resonances fail. However, actors caught up in the meantime may undertake actions that reinforce the Resonances, making them last beyond the Attainment.<br /> <br /> Anyone affected by a summoned Resonance gains a dice bonus equal to half the historian's Spirit dots (rounded up) on any dice rolls to investigate past events relevant to the Resonance.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 3<br /> <br /> Anyone affected by the summoned Resonances are drawn closer to the moment when the Resonance was present, represented by their temporal sympathy becoming stronger by one level. (The Temporal Sympathy Attainment becomes easier to use on them, while manipulating the sympathies per se becomes harder.) However, Unchanged sympathy cannot be achieved this way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No idea for the 4th and 5th Attainments! Maybe something like summoning spirits from the past?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Typo 08-29-2023, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T20:01:27-07:00","id":1521640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1521637#post1521637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's see. <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> notes that Acanthus view Spirit as the forbidden places in the stories and the darkness beyond the light. So, Acanthus who view history as strange times in a strange land would lean to Spirit as means of interacting with the spirits that actually lived through history, and familiarizing herself with that unfamiliar world.<br /> <br /> With a theme like above, something like......<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>First</b><br /> <br /> The historian inquires a spirit's history as Know Spirit (Spirit \u2022), but with the list of available facts expanded to include the following:<br /> <br /> <i>\u2022 How long, roughly, has the spirit been here, and has it ever Manifested or fell into slumber in the meantime?<br /> <br /> \u2022 What actions, broadly, has the spirit taken here?</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u2022 How has the spirit, if ever, changed in Rank or Influences?</i><br /> <br /> Notably, the first time a historian inquires a spirit via this Attainment, she always gets an answer to one of the above expanded questions (chosen by the player) in addition to whatever this Attainment's Potency allows for, circumventing Withstand.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 1<br /> <br /> When inquiring the above expanded questions, the historian may now pin-point when it happened. This cannot circumvent lacunae; if one has happened between the historian's inquiry and the relevant event's true moment of happening, the Attainment provides the lacuna as the answer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Second</b><br /> <br /> The historian awakens the spirits to relive the past. This functions as Coaxing the Spirits (Spirit \u2022), but instead of acting in accordance with its nature, the spirit or its representation reenacts a past action to its best ability. Reach is assigned to instant casting and sensory range.<br /> <br /> The reenactment is performed on the spot; if a spirit clawed at a human, for example, it will make clawing gestures in thin air instead of flying off to maim the original victim again.<br /> <br /> The historian must specify the exact past action he wants to see reenacted. Alternatively, he may designate a past moment, and have the subject reenact what it did in that moment.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 2<br /> <br /> After coaxing the subject, the historian may trigger a vision as per Postcognition (Time \u2022), with Reach assigned to instant casting and retaining awareness (Defense) in the present. Temporal Sympathy can be applied as usual.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Third</b><br /> <br /> Resonance is the means by which the world connects Once and Now, and the historian works to encourage it. She may spend 1 Mana to 'summon' past Resonances of an area, with a ritual that takes time as her Gnosis-derived ritual interval. (Quick reference: three hours at Gnosis 1, one hour at Gnosis 3, thirty minutes at Gnosis 5, ten minutes at Gnosis 7, and one minute at Gnosis 9)<br /> <br /> The summoning lasts for hours equal to the historian's Spirit dots, during which mundane attempts to weaken the summoned Resonances fail. However, actors caught up in the meantime may undertake actions that reinforce the Resonances, making them last beyond the Attainment.<br /> <br /> Anyone affected by a summoned Resonance gains a dice bonus equal to half the historian's Spirit dots (rounded up) on any dice rolls to investigate past events relevant to the Resonance.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 3<br /> <br /> Anyone affected by the summoned Resonances are drawn closer to the moment when the Resonance was present, represented by their temporal sympathy becoming stronger by one level. (The Temporal Sympathy Attainment becomes easier to use on them, while manipulating the sympathies per se becomes harder.) However, Unchanged sympathy cannot be achieved this way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No idea for the 4th and 5th Attainments! Maybe something like summoning spirits from the past?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spam filters turned the post into spam as I attempted to edit one thing, so here\u2019s a quiclnpatchwork solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T07:20:20-07:00","id":1523464,"title":"","content":"Thanks again everyone for the help.<br /> <br /> So I was running a story regarding a grimoire that originated from the Library of the Dead from Gloria Mundi 7 - Descent. The librarian there sent a Retriever (Stygian Supernal Mechanical Spider) to retrieve the grimoire when the previous possessor had stolen it, but the Retriever was sucked into the Abyss before it could complete it's mission. The player characters are in the Library of the Dead right now and the Moros in the group has summoned the Retriever, but now it is tainted by the Abyss and attempted to steal more books from the Library to bring them into the Abyss to &quot;share them&quot;. The characters defeated the Spider and chopped of its legs, but now would like to clear the taint of the Abyss from the Spider (and then repair it) as a favor to the librarian.<br /> <br /> My question is: How can you remove the Abyssal influence from something once it has been corrupted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T09:13:05-07:00","id":1523467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1523464#post1523464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is: How can you remove the Abyssal influence from something once it has been corrupted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Find another creature to do the job you needed the Retriever for or hope for a miracle, because usually if a Supernal being gets eaten by the Abyss it's gone. The closest thing to an established solution to this involves Imperium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T08:05:31-07:00","id":1523497,"title":"","content":"Well, is there any clever way for the Supernal to have somehow survived its trip to the Abyss, because I've already allowed it's resummoning? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T13:37:49-07:00","id":1523509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1523497#post1523497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, is there any clever way for the Supernal to have somehow survived its trip to the Abyss, because I've already allowed it's resummoning? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If they've summoned it again, does that not imply that it somehow got back to the Supernal? I mean, you could have it be a one-off event that is just inexplicable. It's not like your characters in a place to find out.<br /> <br /> Though, given it's behaviour, that would imply that there's now an Abyssal-tainted entity existing inside the Supernal, which is... not great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T15:55:38-07:00","id":1523515,"title":"","content":"Alternatively; Your mages have unwittingly figured out a method to really summon \u2018dead\u2019 Supernal Entities from the Abyss. Local Guardians and Scelesti will become <b>very</b> interested in you once word of this gets<br /> out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T20:00:26-07:00","id":1523522,"title":"","content":"What about this thing being some sort of Abyssal echo of the Supernal that was consumed?<br /> <br /> Btw, the reason it could be resummoned is that it encoded some of itself in the grimoire before being sucked into the Abyss if that helps...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T11:59:05-07:00","id":1523566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1523522#post1523522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about this thing being some sort of Abyssal echo of the Supernal that was consumed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would that not make it a little hard to cleanse? Like, it's no longer the Supernal it was, it's just another Abyssal entity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T12:10:57-07:00","id":1523567,"title":"","content":"Maybe this entity is part of a hive-mind? The one they saw die was a different iteration to the one they've summoned, but the second knows everything the first did, up until the moment the Abyss took the first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T15:59:11-07:00","id":1523972,"title":"","content":"That's a cool idea. Thanks. <br /> <br /> Btw, it seems that people assume that Supernals are always destroyed in the Abyss, but the book indicates that an Abyssal entity might collect one. How do people here feel about this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 10-11-2023, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T19:17:29-07:00","id":1523984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1523972#post1523972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, it seems that people assume that Supernals are always destroyed in the Abyss, but the book indicates that an Abyssal entity might collect one. How do people here feel about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>The immediate next sentence describes the result as a &quot;death,&quot; and Nameless &amp; Accursed describes Greater Tulpa's seeming exception to this &quot;perishing&quot; as specifically ambiguous re: whether it's a new being or the same one somehow rescued from the Abyss.<br /> <br /> The Abyss itself is described consistently as abhorring meaning, and Mage is a gameline where high-level metaphysics include &quot;these different beings are all aspects of this grander-scale being,&quot; &quot;if this thing kills you, it owns your likeness,&quot; and &quot;the Abyss's ability to allow Paradoxical beings to inhabit it comes with a hefty dose of fundamental wrongness that is the same reason it interferes with the Supernal as a force of description of the Phenomenal World.&quot;<br /> <br /> Supernal beings are magical constructs Phenomenally expressing a raw piece of Supernal Truth. The nature of their origin point makes it difficult to say for sure if a comparison to summoning Oneiric goetia is completely accurate, but the gravity the system affords to their destruction suggests at the very least that when the books consistently describes them as being consumed by the Abyss they are not talking about an act that can be recovered from without invoking a plot device.<br /> <br /> Like Michael said, the most straightforward explanation for the current state of things is that there is now an Abyssal entity using the form previously used by a Supernal entity that was consumed. The Retriever is no longer part of the perfect expression of Truth that it was, and restoring it to its former place in the cosmos would be a matter of at least a story's worth of activity to pull off something adjacent to the act of Ascension. Aswadim and Alienated twist reality into knots trying to manage these sorts of feats under the auspices of bigger issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T12:37:59-07:00","id":1524011,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the amazing answer. My main issue is not blowing up the setting with what I've done. Making the summoned entity an Abyssal imposter seems like the best way forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T18:20:31-07:00","id":1524784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1521637#post1521637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's see. <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> notes that Acanthus view Spirit as the forbidden places in the stories and the darkness beyond the light. So, Acanthus who view history as strange times in a strange land would lean to Spirit as means of interacting with the spirits that actually lived through history, and familiarizing herself with that unfamiliar world.<br /> <br /> With a theme like above, something like......<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>First</b><br /> <br /> The historian inquires a spirit's history as Know Spirit (Spirit \u2022), but with the list of available facts expanded to include the following:<br /> <br /> <i>\u2022 How long, roughly, has the spirit been here, and has it ever Manifested or fell into slumber in the meantime?<br /> <br /> \u2022 What actions, broadly, has the spirit taken here?</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u2022 How has the spirit, if ever, changed in Rank or Influences?</i><br /> <br /> Notably, the first time a historian inquires a spirit via this Attainment, she always gets an answer to one of the above expanded questions (chosen by the player) in addition to whatever this Attainment's Potency allows for, circumventing Withstand.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 1<br /> <br /> When inquiring the above expanded questions, the historian may now pin-point when it happened. This cannot circumvent lacunae; if one has happened between the historian's inquiry and the relevant event's true moment of happening, the Attainment provides the lacuna as the answer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Second</b><br /> <br /> The historian awakens the spirits to relive the past. This functions as Coaxing the Spirits (Spirit \u2022), but instead of acting in accordance with its nature, the spirit or its representation reenacts a past action to its best ability. Reach is assigned to instant casting and sensory range.<br /> <br /> The reenactment is performed on the spot; if a spirit clawed at a human, for example, it will make clawing gestures in thin air instead of flying off to maim the original victim again.<br /> <br /> The historian must specify the exact past action he wants to see reenacted. Alternatively, he may designate a past moment, and have the subject reenact what it did in that moment.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 2<br /> <br /> After coaxing the subject, the historian may trigger a vision as per Postcognition (Time \u2022), with Reach assigned to instant casting and retaining awareness (Defense) in the present. Temporal Sympathy can be applied as usual.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Third</b><br /> <br /> Resonance is the means by which the world connects Once and Now, and the historian works to encourage it. She may spend 1 Mana to 'summon' past Resonances of an area, with a ritual that takes time as her Gnosis-derived ritual interval. (Quick reference: three hours at Gnosis 1, one hour at Gnosis 3, thirty minutes at Gnosis 5, ten minutes at Gnosis 7, and one minute at Gnosis 9)<br /> <br /> The summoning lasts for hours equal to the historian's Spirit dots, during which mundane attempts to weaken the summoned Resonances fail. However, actors caught up in the meantime may undertake actions that reinforce the Resonances, making them last beyond the Attainment.<br /> <br /> Anyone affected by a summoned Resonance gains a dice bonus equal to half the historian's Spirit dots (rounded up) on any dice rolls to investigate past events relevant to the Resonance.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 3<br /> <br /> Anyone affected by the summoned Resonances are drawn closer to the moment when the Resonance was present, represented by their temporal sympathy becoming stronger by one level. (The Temporal Sympathy Attainment becomes easier to use on them, while manipulating the sympathies per se becomes harder.) However, Unchanged sympathy cannot be achieved this way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No idea for the 4th and 5th Attainments! Maybe something like summoning spirits from the past?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have any suggested Oblations or Yantras for The Manifest Zeitgeist Legacy?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T21:46:56-07:00","id":1524787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1524784#post1524784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have any suggested Oblations or Yantras for The Manifest Zeitgeist Legacy?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. How about...<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras</b>: A location the mage has visited the first time but has studied via books, etc. (+1); success on an Academics roll related to the spell (+2), presence of Resonance related to the spell, separate from what a ley line's Mana provides (+1, +2 if potent enough to qualify for the Resonant Condition)<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations</b>: Reciting past events of note in an area; compiling historical anecdotes and episodes; communicating with slumbering spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T17:52:47-07:00","id":1524853,"title":"","content":"Just trying to make sure I understand something correctly for tomorrow night's session:<br /> <br /> A Death Mage (Gnosis 7, Death 5) casts an 8 potency Aggravated Withering Death as an area spell (8 meter cone) with +5 worth of Yantras at some mid-powered Mages with Wards and Signs 6 (which does nothing since it's an area spell).<br /> <br /> This would be + 1 Reach for Aggravated ,+1 Reach for Advanced Area of effect, + 1 Reach for Instant = 1 Reach, 4 Paradox dice - no big deal<br /> <br /> Gnosis 7 + Death 5 + 5 Yantras - 6 extra Potency = 11 dice - almost sure to land on my PCs. The Counterspell clashes are 12 vs. 7 and 12 vs. 6 in favour of the assailant.<br /> <br /> So they all take 8 Aggravated? The Obrimos guy lives only taking 5 due to Mage armor. Mastigos w/Prime 3 lives only taking 5 from Prime armor. Moros w/Matter lives only taking 5. Unfortunately the Acanthus w/Spirit takes the full 8 Agg and dies.<br /> <br /> Are these the cold hard facts? If the spell were targeted instead, would the Wards and Signs subtract from the Potency of the spell and everyone is ok?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.<br /> <br /> PS: How do you think Arm Ghost from 1st edition would work in 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 10-31-2023, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T19:32:42-07:00","id":1524856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1524853#post1524853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are these the cold hard facts? If the spell were targeted instead, would the Wards and Signs subtract from the Potency of the spell and everyone is ok?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what Wards and Signs is saying is that a spell that doesn't directly act on the target isn't Withstood, not that using Area factors makes its defenses invalid \u2014 it's the same &quot;spells with temporary effects can still have Lasting consequences&quot; as a spell that starts a fire still being able to burn things that are resistant to magic. Wither is a spell that affects targets, not a spell that creates an effect; to use an example from the same page as Wards and Signs, simply casting Aetheric Winds on an area (no frills) wouldn't bypass the ward, but the Reach effect to create the Heavy Winds Tilt in the area would produce after-effects that the magic wouldn't mitigate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T23:20:16-07:00","id":1524862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1524853#post1524853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just trying to make sure I understand something correctly for tomorrow night's session:<br /> <br /> A Death Mage (Gnosis 7, Death 5) casts an 8 potency Aggravated Withering Death as an area spell (8 meter cone) with +5 worth of Yantras at some mid-powered Mages with Wards and Signs 6 (which does nothing since it's an area spell).<br /> <br /> This would be + 1 Reach for Aggravated ,+1 Reach for Advanced Area of effect, + 1 Reach for Instant = 1 Reach, 4 Paradox dice - no big deal<br /> <br /> Gnosis 7 + Death 5 + 5 Yantras - 6 extra Potency = 11 dice - almost sure to land on my PCs. The Counterspell clashes are 12 vs. 7 and 12 vs. 6 in favour of the assailant.<br /> <br /> So they all take 8 Aggravated? The Obrimos guy lives only taking 5 due to Mage armor. Mastigos w/Prime 3 lives only taking 5 from Prime armor. Moros w/Matter lives only taking 5. Unfortunately the Acanthus w/Spirit takes the full 8 Agg and dies.<br /> <br /> Are these the cold hard facts? If the spell were targeted instead, would the Wards and Signs subtract from the Potency of the spell and everyone is ok?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.<br /> <br /> PS: How do you think Arm Ghost from 1st edition would work in 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, Withering's exact effect in the narrative still requires the spell to target a specific someone, even if 'specific' means 'everyone in this area' (as opposed to &quot;rot the air&quot; or something like that), so Wards and Signs should work.<br /> <br /> <br /> Arm Ghost is a bit harder to pull off if trying to build off the existing 2e spells that do similar things, Primal Transfer and Hung Spell. You could homebrew things so that those spells are contorted to somehow benefit ghosts via Death add-ons and Reaches<br /> <br /> Or homebrew a new version of Arm Ghost that does what it does in ie. I wouldn't make it Death 3, though! Probably Death 4 + Prime 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T01:52:26-07:00","id":1524866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095319-chronicle-help?p=1524853#post1524853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just trying to make sure I understand something correctly for tomorrow night's session:</div> </div> </div> </div>As already mentioned twice, Wards and Signs does still apply.<br /> <br /> Also, the Moros using Matter Armour should also take full (2 after Withstand) damage. Matter Armour as described should only protect from external physical attacks. Withering affects the subject's body directly, making any changes to surrounding materia irrelevant.<br /> <br /> The rest of the math looks ok to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T16:28:33-07:00","id":1524890,"title":"","content":"Ok. Thanks everyone. All that makes sense. I'll likely boost the damage to 10 Agg for 7 dice then. That way most PCs will take 1 - 4 Agg. Arm Ghost I'll say is Death 4 Prime 3 since the Ghost doesn't permanently get imbued. More like a potion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T16:46:31-08:00","id":1525137,"title":"","content":"Anyone have any advice for what a Cryptologos tutor would want a pupil to discover to be inducted into the Legacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T12:45:40-08:00","id":1525175,"title":"","content":"That would depend on their Order. I assume the Mysterium is far more strict about exchange of knowledge than the Free Council is. The latter might not even require any supernatural discoveries - just creation of something to benefit the Sleepers, like translating literature between two languages, refining translation software, leading lectures, acting as an interpreter or advancing mundane understanding of languages, both ancient land living.<br /> <br /> Actual Mysteries involving the Cryptologos might involve:<br /> + Showing progress on learning an occult language, like a dialect of High Speech, First Tongue or Iremite.<br /> + Visiting the realm of language in the Astral, and writing down observations of the Omphalos.<br /> + Translating a Grimoire or records from a lost language, like Minoan Linear A.<br /> + Identifying covert communications, like pipes in a local basement creaking in Morse code.<br /> + Capturing the white snake from the German fairy tale, whose flesh lets you communicate with animals.<br /> + On the local lake, the reeds repeat secrets that have been whispered to them, like in the other story of Midas.<br /> + Affect the workings of Acad\u00e9mie Fran\u00e7aise, the French deciding body on the matters of language and track the consequences.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}